            <!-- ─────────── PRACTICE DRILL 2.5 ─────────── -->
            <div class="cka-practice-drill">
                <h4>🔬 Practice Drill 2.5 — Kubelet Won't Start: the cgroup-Driver Mismatch</h4>
                <div class="drill-timer">⏱️ Target Time: 7 minutes</div>
                <div class="drill-scenario">
                    <h5>Scenario</h5>
                    <p>A freshly provisioned node refuses to join: <code>systemctl status kubelet</code> shows a crash-loop and the journal mentions cgroups. Diagnose the classic cause — the kubelet and containerd disagree on the cgroup <em>driver</em> — and fix both sides to <code>systemd</code>.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="drill-hint">
                    <strong>Hint:</strong> containerd's default is <code>cgroupfs</code>; kubeadm clusters expect <code>systemd</code> on both. The containerd side lives in <code>/etc/containerd/config.toml</code> under the runc options; the kubelet side in <code>/var/lib/kubelet/config.yaml</code>.
                </div>
                <div class="drill-solution">
                    <details>
                        <summary>View Solution</summary>
                        <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                            <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-dot red"></span><span class="code-dot yellow"></span><span class="code-dot green"></span><span class="code-lang">diagnose → align both drivers → restart</span></div>
<pre><code class="language-bash"><span class="comment"># 1. DIAGNOSE — read the kubelet's own words</span>
sudo journalctl -u kubelet --no-pager | tail -20
<span class="comment">#   "failed to run Kubelet: misconfiguration: kubelet cgroup driver: \"systemd\"</span>
<span class="comment">#    is different from docker/containerd cgroup driver: \"cgroupfs\""</span>

<span class="comment"># 2. FIX containerd → systemd driver</span>
sudo sed -i 's/SystemdCgroup = false/SystemdCgroup = true/' /etc/containerd/config.toml
<span class="comment">#   ([plugins."io.containerd.grpc.v1.cri".containerd.runtimes.runc.options])</span>

<span class="comment"># 3. CONFIRM the kubelet side matches (kubeadm default is already systemd)</span>
grep cgroupDriver /var/lib/kubelet/config.yaml     <span class="comment"># cgroupDriver: systemd</span>

<span class="comment"># 4. RESTART the pair, runtime first</span>
sudo systemctl restart containerd
sudo systemctl restart kubelet

<span class="comment"># 5. VERIFY</span>
sudo systemctl is-active containerd kubelet        <span class="comment"># active active ✅</span>
kubectl get nodes                                  <span class="comment"># node Ready ✅</span></code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <p><strong>Check yourself:</strong> the kubelet and the runtime <em>both</em> write cgroup limits for containers, so they must speak the same dialect — <code>systemd</code> on modern distros. The journal names the mismatch outright, the fix is one line of TOML, and the restart order is runtime-then-kubelet. Bonus fact for v1.35+: the node must also be on cgroups <strong>v2</strong> (v1 is deprecated) — check with <code>stat -fc %T /sys/fs/cgroup/</code> (<code>cgroup2fs</code> = good).</p>
                    </details>
                </div>
            </div>

