                <h4>Three Cluster Topologies — How the Same Components Get Arranged</h4>
                <p>Every cluster has the same components; what varies is <strong>how many copies and where they live</strong>. You'll build the first topology in Ch 9 and the HA ones in Ch 35 — but knowing all three <em>now</em> makes every "how many nodes / what fails when" question answerable:</p>
                <div class="diagram-container">
                    <div class="diagram-title">Single control plane → stacked HA → external etcd</div>
<pre>
  ① SINGLE CONTROL PLANE (learning / dev — what kubeadm init gives you)
     ┌────────── CP node ──────────┐    ┌─ worker ─┐ ┌─ worker ─┐
     │ apiserver·etcd·sched·c-mgr  │    │  pods    │ │  pods    │
     └─────────────────────────────┘    └──────────┘ └──────────┘
     💥 CP node dies → no API, no scheduling (pods keep running "headless")

  ② STACKED HA (production default — etcd rides ON each CP node)
     ┌── CP-1 ──┐ ┌── CP-2 ──┐ ┌── CP-3 ──┐      🔀 LB in front of :6443
     │ api+etcd │ │ api+etcd │ │ api+etcd │      etcd quorum = 2 of 3
     └──────────┘ └──────────┘ └──────────┘      lose 1 CP node → still healthy
     ⚠️ each CP loss costs an apiserver AND an etcd member at once

  ③ EXTERNAL ETCD (large/critical clusters — etcd on its own machines)
     ┌─ CP-1 ─┐ ┌─ CP-2 ─┐ ┌─ CP-3 ─┐   ┌─ etcd-1 ─┐ ┌─ etcd-2 ─┐ ┌─ etcd-3 ─┐
     │ api…   │ │ api…   │ │ api…   │──▶│          │ │          │ │          │
     └────────┘ └────────┘ └────────┘   └──────────┘ └──────────┘ └──────────┘
     failure domains SEPARATED (6+ machines) — an apiserver loss never touches etcd
</pre>
                </div>
                <table>
                    <thead><tr><th>Topology</th><th>Machines (min)</th><th>Survives</th><th>Use when</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td>① Single CP</td><td>1 CP + workers</td><td>nothing (CP is a SPOF)</td><td>learning, dev, the exam's practice clusters</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>② Stacked HA</td><td>3 CP + workers</td><td>1 CP-node loss</td><td>the standard production choice</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>③ External etcd</td><td>3 CP + 3 etcd</td><td>1 of each, independently</td><td>large clusters where etcd needs its own I/O &amp; blast radius</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
                <div class="info-box tip mb-0">
                    <h5>💡 Why always an odd number of etcd members?</h5>
                    <p class="mb-0">etcd commits a write only when a <strong>majority</strong> (quorum) agrees: 3 members tolerate 1 failure (quorum 2), 5 tolerate 2 (quorum 3). An <em>even</em> count adds cost but no extra failure tolerance — 4 members still only tolerate 1 loss (quorum 3) and can split 2–2. Hence 1, 3, or 5 — never 2 or 4. Full quorum math in Ch 35.</p>
                </div>
