                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number">Q4</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">The scheduler is down. What symptom appears, and on which objects?</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Answer</summary>
                        <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                        <p><strong>New pods stay <code>Pending</code></strong> (no node gets assigned). Existing pods keep running. Spot it: <code>kubectl get pods -A | grep Pending</code>, then check the scheduler pod/logs.</p>
                        <table>
                            <thead><tr><th>With the scheduler down…</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr><td>❌ new pods: <code>Pending</code>, <code>nodeName</code> empty, <em>no scheduling events</em></td><td>nobody performs the Bind</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>✅ existing pods: unaffected</td><td>already bound — kubelets keep running them</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>✅ kubectl / apiserver: fine</td><td>the scheduler is a <em>consumer</em> of the API, not part of its path</td></tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                        <div class="eq-explanation"><div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div><p>The scheduler only sets <code>nodeName</code>; with it down, pods are created but never bound.</p></div>
