                    <div class="exam-question-item">
                        <span class="eq-number">Q10</span>
                        <div class="eq-question">Draw or describe the complete communication flow between all Kubernetes components when a user runs <code>kubectl delete pod easypj-web</code>. Which components are involved and what happens at each step?</div>
                        <details>
                            <summary>Show Answer</summary>
                                <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                                <p><strong>Pod deletion flow:</strong></p>
<div class="code-block-wrapper">
    <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-dot red"></span><span class="code-dot yellow"></span><span class="code-dot green"></span><span class="code-lang">bash</span></div>
<pre><code class="language-bash">kubectl delete pod easypj-web
        │
        ▼
┌─────────────────┐
│  kube-apiserver  │ ← Receives DELETE request
│  1. Authenticate │
│  2. Authorize    │
│  3. Set deletion │
│     timestamp    │
└────────┬────────┘
         │ Updates etcd: pod.deletionTimestamp = now
         │ pod.deletionGracePeriodSeconds = 30 (default)
         ▼
┌─────────────────┐
│    kubelet       │ ← Watches API, sees deletionTimestamp
│  1. Send SIGTERM │
│  2. Wait 30s     │    to containers
│  3. Send SIGKILL │    (if still running)
│  4. Report back  │
└────────┬────────┘
         │
         ▼
┌─────────────────┐
│  kube-apiserver  │ ← kubelet confirms termination
│  Remove from     │
│  etcd            │
└─────────────────┘
         │
         ▼
┌─────────────────┐
│ Endpoint ctrl    │ ← Removes pod IP from Service endpoints
└─────────────────┘</code></pre>
</div>
                            <div class="eq-explanation">
                                <div class="eq-exp-label">Explanation</div>
                                <p>Key points for the CKA: (1) Deletion is <strong>graceful</strong> by default — containers get SIGTERM and 30 seconds to shut down. (2) The <code>--grace-period=0 --force</code> flags skip the grace period (useful for stuck pods). (3) The Endpoint controller removes the pod from Service endpoints <em>concurrently</em> with the grace period, so in-flight requests may still reach a terminating pod. (4) <code>preStop</code> hooks run before SIGTERM — use them for graceful shutdown logic. Understanding pod lifecycle is critical for troubleshooting stuck deletions and graceful application shutdown.</p>
                            </div>
                        </details>
                    </div>
            </div>

            
