                    <div class="info-card">
                        <div class="card-icon-lg">📊</div>
                        <h5>Observability</h5>
                        <p>Logs, metrics, and audit records (Ch 28, 29) — but the official docs add a subtle point: review the <em>whole chain</em> that populates a dashboard, not just the dashboard itself, and for high-assurance environments, make audit logs tamper-proof and confidential, not just present.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <h4>The Official Kubernetes Security Checklist — A Concrete Starting Point</h4>
                <p>Beyond the two mental models above, the official docs also publish a genuinely practical artifact at <code>kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/security/security-checklist/</code>: eight concrete categories you can walk, cluster by cluster, control by control. It's the closest thing kubernetes.io has to "here's literally what to go check" — and it maps almost one-to-one onto this guide's own chapter structure:</p>
