                        <div class="card-icon-lg">🚨</div>
                        <h5>CVE-2020-8554 — A Checklist Line You Can Name a CVE For</h5>
                        <p>The checklist's "restrict use of <code>LoadBalancer</code> and <code>ExternalIPs</code>" line exists because of a real, disclosed vulnerability: any user permitted to create or update Services could set an arbitrary <code>externalIPs</code> value and redirect other users' cluster traffic to their own endpoint — a man-in-the-middle with no exploit required beyond an over-permissive RBAC grant. There is no complete server-side fix; the mitigation is restricting who may set <code>externalIPs</code> at all (RBAC) or blocking the field outright with the <code>DenyServiceExternalIPs</code> admission controller.</p>
