                <p>Kubernetes attacks have not stayed static. They have evolved through four distinct eras, each building on the lessons of the previous one. Understanding this progression is critical because <strong>every attack pattern from every era still works today</strong> on unhardened clusters. Attackers don't abandon old techniques — they layer new ones on top.</p>
