                        <div class="step-content">
                            <p><strong>Era 1 (2018) — Exposed Dashboards:</strong> Kubernetes Dashboard shipped with <code>--enable-skip-login</code> and cluster-admin privileges by default in many distributions. Attackers used Shodan to find port 6443 or 8001 and walked straight in — no exploit needed, just a browser. <strong>CKS response:</strong> Chapters 5 (Dashboard auth), 8 (API server hardening), and 9 (RBAC).</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="process-step-item">
