                        <div class="step-content">
                            <p><strong>Era 2 (2019) — Cloud Metadata SSRF:</strong> As organizations moved to the cloud, a new attack surface emerged: the metadata API at <code>169.254.169.254</code>. Every pod on every EC2 node can reach this IP by default — a single SSRF vulnerability yields the node's IAM role credentials. Capital One's $270M breach was this exact pattern. <strong>CKS response:</strong> Chapters 13 (metadata concealment), 16 (IAM minimization), and 6 (NetworkPolicy egress).</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="process-step-item">
