                    <h5>① CVSS Anatomy — How Attack Vectors Get Ranked, and Why "Network + No Auth" Always Wins the Priority Fight</h5>
                    <p>§2.1's severity heat map used percentages from penetration-testing data, but the security industry has a formal, universal scoring system for exactly this ranking problem: <strong>CVSS (Common Vulnerability Scoring System)</strong>. You don't need to memorize CVSS math for the CKS exam, but understanding its four core metrics explains <em>why</em> an exposed API server (Vector 1) is always fixed before a root container (Vector 5) even though both are "critical":</p>
