            <section class="section-block" id="cks-s3-1">
                <h3 class="section-h">3.1 How CKS Security Maps to Kubernetes Components</h3>
                <p>Kubernetes is not one program — it is a <strong>distributed system</strong> of cooperating components, each running as a separate process with its own configuration, its own ports, and its own security surface. Understanding which component owns which security responsibility is the single most important architectural insight for the CKS exam. If you configure a Seccomp profile on the API server, nothing happens — because Seccomp is enforced by the container runtime on worker nodes, not by the API server. These kinds of category errors are exactly what the exam tests for.</p>

                <div class="info-box note">
                    <h5>📖 The CKS Component → Control Mapping</h5>
                    <p>Every security control in the CKS curriculum is enforced by exactly ONE Kubernetes component. Your job as a CKS administrator is to know which component to configure for which control. The diagram below is the master map — return to it whenever you are unsure where a control lives.</p>
                </div>

                <h4>Kubernetes Security Architecture — Components + Controls</h4>
                <div class="diagram-container">
                    <div class="diagram-title">Every CKS control mapped to its enforcement component</div>
<pre>
  🔐 CONTROL PLANE
  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │
  │  │  🌐 kube-apiserver (port 6443)                            │  │
  │  │  The GATEKEEPER. EVERY request passes through here.       │  │
  │  │  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │  │
  │  │  │ Authentication → "Who are you?"                     │ │  │
  │  │  │   • X.509 client certificates (kubeconfig)          │ │  │
  │  │  │   • ServiceAccount JWT tokens                       │ │  │
  │  │  │   • OIDC (Google, GitHub, Azure AD) — Ch 5          │ │  │
  │  │  │   • Bootstrap tokens (node join)                    │ │  │
  │  │  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤ │  │
  │  │  │ Authorization → "What can you do?"                  │ │  │
  │  │  │   • RBAC (Role/ClusterRole + Binding) — Ch 9        │ │  │
  │  │  │   • Node authorizer (kubelet restrictions) — Ch 11  │ │  │
  │  │  │   • Webhook mode (external policy decisions)        │ │  │
  │  │  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤ │  │
  │  │  │ Admission Control → "Is this request allowed?"      │ │  │
  │  │  │   • Pod Security Standards — Ch 17                  │ │  │
  │  │  │   • OPA/Gatekeeper — Ch 24                          │ │  │
  │  │  │   • ImagePolicyWebhook — Ch 23, 24                  │ │  │
  │  │  │   • AlwaysPullImages — Ch 8, NodeRestriction — Ch 11│ │  │
  │  │  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤ │  │
  │  │  │ Audit Logging → "Record what happened"              │ │  │
  │  │  │   • --audit-policy-file — Ch 28                     │ │  │
  │  │  │   • --audit-log-path, --audit-log-maxage            │ │  │
  │  │  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │  │
  │  └────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘  │
  │                           │ TLS (--etcd-certfile)                │
  │  ┌────────────────────────▼──────────────────────────────────┐  │
  │  │  🗄️ etcd (port 2379)                                       │  │
  │  │  The BRAIN. Stores ALL cluster state + ALL Secrets.        │  │
  │  │  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │  │
  │  │  │ Encryption at Rest → "Secrets unreadable on disk"   │  │  │
  │  │  │   • --encryption-provider-config — Ch 19            │  │  │
  │  │  │   • AES-CBC, AES-GCM, KMS plugins                   │  │  │
  │  │  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤  │  │
  │  │  │ Network Isolation → "Only API server can connect"   │  │  │
  │  │  │   • --peer-cert-file (mTLS between etcd peers)      │  │  │
  │  │  │   • --cert-file, --key-file (server TLS)            │  │  │
  │  │  │   • Firewall: restrict port 2379 to API server IP   │  │  │
  │  │  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤  │  │
