                <div class="drill-hint">
                    <strong>Hint:</strong> TLS → AuthN → AuthZ → Admission (split into 4a Mutating / 4b Validating) → Audit. The circled gate should be Admission — GET/LIST requests never mutate state, so there's nothing to admit.
                </div>
                <div class="drill-solution">
                    <details>
                        <summary>View Solution</summary>
                        <table>
                            <thead><tr><th>Gate</th><th>Owner</th><th>Failure signal</th><th>Chapter</th></tr></thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr><td>1 — TLS</td><td>kube-apiserver (transport)</td><td>TLS handshake error</td><td>7, 8</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>2 — AuthN</td><td>kube-apiserver (authn chain)</td><td>401 Unauthorized</td><td>8, 10</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>3 — AuthZ</td><td>kube-apiserver (authz chain: Node→RBAC→Webhook)</td><td>403 Forbidden, no policy reason</td><td>9, 11</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>4a — Mutating Admission</td><td>MutatingWebhookConfigurations</td><td>silent — fields appear you didn't write</td><td>24</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>4b — Validating Admission</td><td>PSS, OPA/Gatekeeper, Kyverno, ImagePolicyWebhook</td><td>403 Forbidden WITH a policy reason</td><td>17, 23, 24</td></tr>
                                <tr><td>5 — Audit</td><td>kube-apiserver (audit backend)</td><td>never blocks — only records</td><td>28</td></tr>
