            <!-- ─────────── VISUAL SUMMARY ─────────── -->
            <span class="ch-jump" id="cks-ch3-cheatsheet"></span>
            <div class="visual-summary">
                <div class="diagram-title">⚡ Ch 3 Visual Cheat Sheet — Security Architecture</div>
                <div class="card-grid cols-4">
                    <div class="info-card"><div class="card-icon-lg">🔐</div><h5>Gate 1: TLS</h5><p>Is the channel encrypted and trusted? Mutual TLS, client/server certs. Fail → handshake error, not even a 401.</p></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><div class="card-icon-lg">🚪</div><h5>Gate 2: AuthN</h5><p>Who are you? X.509 certs, OIDC, Webhook tokens. Anonymous if disabled.</p></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><div class="card-icon-lg">🔑</div><h5>Gate 3: AuthZ</h5><p>What can you do? RBAC, Node Authorizer, ABAC, Webhook. Deny by default.</p></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><div class="card-icon-lg">🔀</div><h5>Gate 4a: Mutating Admission</h5><p>Can modify request. Inject sidecars, add defaults. Runs BEFORE validating.</p></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><div class="card-icon-lg">✅</div><h5>Gate 4b: Validating Admission</h5><p>Accept or reject. OPA/Gatekeeper, Kyverno, PSS. Runs AFTER mutating.</p></div>
