                </div>
                <div class="vs-prose">
                    <p class="mb-0">Every kubectl command that mutates state passes through all five gates in a fixed order — TLS mutual auth, then AuthN (who you are), AuthZ (what you can do), Admission's mutating-then-validating pair (default injection, then accept/reject), and finally Audit logging (the permanent record). Read-only GET/LIST calls skip Gate 4 only; everything else always runs.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

