        <article class="chapter" id="cks-ch4">
            <div class="chapter-intro">
            <h2 class="chapter-title">Chapter 4 · CIS Benchmarks &amp; kube-bench — Measuring Your Security Baseline</h2>
            <p class="chapter-lead">Before you can harden a Kubernetes cluster, you must <strong>measure it</strong>. You cannot fix what you cannot see. The CIS Kubernetes Benchmark is the industry-standard checklist — over 200 security configuration tests covering every component: the API server, etcd, kubelet, controller manager, scheduler, and worker nodes. The tool that automates these checks is <strong>kube-bench</strong>. This chapter teaches you to run kube-bench, interpret every FAIL and WARN result, and apply the exact fix — editing the right configuration file, adding the right flag, and verifying the fix. Every CKS hardening task traces back to a CIS check.</p>
            <div class="chapter-meta">
                <span class="meta-tag">🟢 Beginner</span>
                <span class="meta-tag">⏱️ ~2 hours</span>
                <span class="meta-tag">🔧 Hands-On</span>
                <span class="meta-tag">📏 CIS Standards</span>
            </div>
            </div><!-- /chapter-intro -->

            <div class="learning-objectives">
                <h4>🎯 What You'll Learn</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>✅ Understand what CIS Benchmarks are and why they are the foundation of K8s security auditing</li>
                    <li>✅ Install and run kube-bench against control plane and worker nodes</li>
                    <li>✅ Interpret PASS/FAIL/WARN output and map each result to the configuration file you must edit</li>
                    <li>✅ Fix the most common API server CIS failures by editing <code>/etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-apiserver.yaml</code></li>
                    <li>✅ Harden the kubelet by editing <code>/var/lib/kubelet/config.yaml</code> — disable anonymous auth, enable webhook authorization</li>
                    <li>✅ Apply the top 5 highest-impact CIS fixes to the easypj cluster and verify each with a kube-bench re-run</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="cka-chapter-relevance">
                <span class="relevance-label">🎓 CKS Relevance</span>
                <div class="relevance-domains">
                    <span class="cka-domain-badge">Cluster Setup <span class="cka-weight">10%</span></span>
                    <span class="cka-domain-badge">Cluster Hardening <span class="cka-weight">15%</span></span>
                    <span class="cka-domain-badge">System Hardening <span class="cka-weight">15%</span></span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="cka-exam-tip">
                <h5>🧠 The kube-bench → Fix Pattern</h5>
