            <!-- ─────────── PRACTICE DRILL 6.3 ─────────── -->
            <div class="cka-practice-drill">
                <h4>🔬 Practice Drill 6.3 — Replay the §6.1 Lateral-Movement Attack Chain and Prove Each Policy Blocks One Step</h4>
                <div class="drill-timer">⏱️ Target Time: 10 minutes</div>
                <div class="drill-scenario">
                    <h5>Scenario</h5>
                    <p>Reusing the cluster from Drill 6.2 (or rebuild it): BEFORE applying any policies, replay each of the 4 steps from §6.1's "Lateral Movement Without NetworkPolicies" diagram (discovery, database access, cache poisoning, cross-namespace scan) as literal commands from the <code>easypj</code> pod, and confirm each one SUCCEEDS. Then apply the 6 policies one at a time, in the order 1→6, and after each one, re-attempt only the attack steps that policy is supposed to newly block.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="drill-hint">
                    <strong>Hint:</strong> Policy 1 (default-deny) should immediately kill ALL 4 steps at once — that's the point of starting with deny-all. Policies 2-6 then re-open only the narrow paths the app legitimately needs, and none of the 4 attack steps should come back.</div>
                <div class="drill-solution">
                    <details>
                        <summary>View Solution</summary>
                        <table>
                            <thead><tr><th>§6.1 Attack Step</th><th>Command From easypj Pod</th><th>Before Any Policy</th><th>After Policy 1 (default-deny)</th><th>After Policies 2-6</th></tr></thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr><td>1. Discovery via env vars</td><td><code>env \| grep _SERVICE_HOST</code></td><td>✅ succeeds (env vars always injected)</td><td>✅ still succeeds — env vars aren't network traffic</td><td>✅ still succeeds — NetworkPolicy can't hide env vars, only block the connection they'd enable</td></tr>
