                    <p><strong>In words:</strong> Kubernetes ships with a flat network — every pod can reach every other pod on every port until you add NetworkPolicies. The 7 essential patterns (default-deny ingress/egress, allow-port, allow-namespace, allow-CIDR, allow-DNS, allow-same-namespace) are the building blocks; the easypj implementation combines six of them into one complete zero-trust policy set: default-deny, then explicit exceptions for the database, the ingress controller, the cache, DNS, and monitoring.</p>
