                <div class="drill-timer">⏱️ Target Time: 10 minutes</div>
                <div class="drill-scenario">
                    <h5>Scenario</h5>
                    <p>Reusing a kind cluster with Calico and cert-manager installed: apply Chapter 6's <code>default-deny-ingress</code> NetworkPolicy to the namespace BEFORE requesting any certificate, then create a <code>Certificate</code> using an HTTP-01 solver and confirm it gets stuck exactly as described in this section's Q3. Apply Q3's <code>allow-acme-http01-solver</code> NetworkPolicy and confirm the same <code>Certificate</code> reaches <code>Ready</code> without ever touching the original deny-all policy.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="drill-hint">
                    <strong>Hint:</strong> <code>kubectl get pods -l acme.cert-manager.io/http01-solver=true</code> shows the ephemeral solver pod cert-manager creates — inspect its labels directly rather than guessing them.</div>
