                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number">Q2</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">What's the difference between a Role+RoleBinding and a ClusterRole+RoleBinding? When would you use the latter?</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Answer</summary>
                    <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                    <p><strong>Role+RoleBinding:</strong> Role defines permissions in ONE namespace. RoleBinding binds it in the SAME namespace. <strong>ClusterRole+RoleBinding:</strong> ClusterRole defines permissions cluster-wide (or for cluster-scoped resources like nodes). The RoleBinding still binds it in ONE namespace, but the subject gets the ClusterRole's permissions IN THAT NAMESPACE ONLY. Use when: you want to reuse the same permission set across multiple namespaces (one ClusterRole, multiple RoleBindings).</p>
                    </details>
                </div>
                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number">Q3</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">A ServiceAccount needs to read pods in ALL namespaces. Write the minimal ClusterRole and ClusterRoleBinding.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Answer</summary>
                    <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
<pre><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: ClusterRole
metadata:
  name: all-pods-reader
rules:
- apiGroups: [""]
  resources: ["pods"]
  verbs: ["get", "list", "watch"]
---
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: ClusterRoleBinding
metadata:
  name: monitoring-all-pods
subjects:
- kind: ServiceAccount
  name: monitoring-sa
  namespace: monitoring
roleRef:
  kind: ClusterRole
  name: all-pods-reader
  apiGroup: rbac.authorization.k8s.io</code></pre>
