                <h4>Decision Tree: Does My Pod Need API Access?</h4>
                <p>Walk through this decision tree for every pod in your cluster. The most common CKS mistake is either disabling the token on a pod that needs it (breaking functionality) or leaving the token mounted on a pod that does not need it (leaving a credential exposed):</p>
                <div class="decision-tree">
                    <div class="decision-node question">🔍 Does this pod call the Kubernetes API? (kubectl, client-go, any /api/ endpoint?)</div>
                    <div class="decision-branches">
                        <div><div class="decision-node no">❌ NO → automountServiceAccountToken: false. Create a dedicated SA with zero RBAC. The easypj web app does NOT call the K8s API — it serves HTTP.</div></div>
                        <div><div class="decision-node yes">✅ YES → Continue. The pod needs a token.</div></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="decision-node question">📋 Does it need read-only access (get/list/watch) to specific resources?</div>
                    <div class="decision-branches">
                        <div><div class="decision-node yes">✅ YES → Create dedicated SA + Role with only get/list/watch on only the needed resources. Example: easypj-operator-sa → ConfigMaps only.</div></div>
                        <div><div class="decision-node no">❌ NO → Continue.</div></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="decision-node question">✏️ Does it need to modify resources (create/update/delete)?</div>
                    <div class="decision-branches">
                        <div><div class="decision-node yes">✅ YES → Create dedicated SA + Role with only the needed verbs on only the needed resources. Example: ci-deployer-sa → update deployments only. Use bound tokens with 1-hour expiry.</div></div>
                        <div><div class="decision-node no">🎉 Your pod needs API access but NOT to modify resources. Verify with kubectl auth can-i --list --as=system:serviceaccount:&lt;ns&gt;:&lt;sa&gt;. Every verb listed beyond get/list/watch is a finding.</div></div>
                    </div>
                </div>

