                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number">Q1</span>
                    <div class="eq-question">How do you enable NodeRestriction, and what specific attack does it prevent?</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Answer</summary>
                    <div class="eq-answer-label">Answer</div>
                    <p>Add <code>NodeRestriction</code> to <code>--enable-admission-plugins=...,NodeRestriction</code> in kube-apiserver.yaml. It prevents a compromised kubelet on node01 from: (1) modifying node02's labels/taints (isolation bypass), (2) updating pods on other nodes (cross-node lateral movement), (3) modifying its own node's labels to attract pods from other nodes (pod hijacking).</p>
