                    <p class="mb-0"><strong>In words:</strong> node security is two authorization gates plus a network-layer endpoint that neither gate ever sees. Node Authorizer decides what a kubelet may READ; NodeRestriction decides what it may MODIFY; the metadata service at 169.254.169.254 bypasses both entirely because it's answered by the node's own cloud agent, not the Kubernetes API server — which is exactly why it needs its own dedicated NetworkPolicy and IMDSv2 controls.</p>
