            <p class="chapter-lead">Running an outdated Kubernetes version is not a performance issue — it is a <strong>security vulnerability</strong>. Critical CVEs are disclosed regularly for Kubernetes components. Each CVE is patched in a new version. If you are not upgrading, you are running known vulnerabilities with publicly available exploit code. The CKS exam tests your understanding of the K8s release cycle, the upgrade process using kubeadm, and the security implications of running unsupported versions. This chapter teaches you how to keep your cluster secure through disciplined version management — how to plan upgrades, how to execute them safely, and how to distinguish between urgent security patches and routine minor upgrades.</p>
