                    <li><code>kubectl describe ns prod | grep pod-security</code> — check current PSS labels on a namespace in one line.</li>
                    <li><code>kubectl get ns --show-labels | grep pod-security</code> — see PSS levels across every namespace in the cluster at a glance, useful for spotting a namespace with no PSS labels at all.</li>
                    <li>When fixing a pod for Restricted, apply the golden securityContext block (§17.1 Q9-style: runAsNonRoot, seccompProfile, allowPrivilegeEscalation:false, capabilities.drop:[ALL], readOnlyRootFilesystem) as one paste — don't chase violations field-by-field under time pressure.</li>
