            <section class="section-block" id="s23-3">
                <h3 class="section-h">23.3 Trivy — Image Vulnerability Scanner Deep Dive</h3>
                <p>Trivy is the <strong>de facto standard</strong> open-source vulnerability scanner for containers, developed by Aqua Security. It's fast (scans in seconds), comprehensive (detects CVEs in OS packages AND language-specific dependencies), and free. The CKS exam expects you to scan an image and interpret the output. But to truly understand Trivy, you need to understand <strong>how it works under the hood</strong> — the vulnerability database, the matching algorithm, and the CI/CD integration patterns.</p>

