                    <div class="info-card"><div class="card-icon-lg">📜</div><h5>OPA / Rego</h5><p><code>violation[&#123;"msg": msg&#125;]</code> pattern. ConstraintTemplate = logic, Constraint = parameters.</p></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><div class="card-icon-lg">🏛️</div><h5>Kyverno</h5><p>Pure YAML. Validate / Mutate / Generate / VerifyImages, all built in.</p></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><div class="card-icon-lg">📖</div><h5>Defaults (24.5)</h5><p>PodSecurity, ServiceAccount, ValidatingAdmissionPolicy = ON. NodeRestriction, ImagePolicyWebhook = OFF.</p></div>
                </div>
                <div class="vs-prose">
                    <p><strong>In words:</strong> every admission request passes through mutating plugins/webhooks first (sequential, can modify), then validating plugins/webhooks second (parallel, accept-or-reject only) — <code>failurePolicy</code> decides what happens if a webhook is unreachable when its turn comes.</p>
                    <p class="mb-0"><strong>The takeaway:</strong> OPA Gatekeeper (Rego) and Kyverno (YAML) are the two dominant ways to plug custom logic into that pipeline — and before you write either one, check §24.5's default table so you don't reinvent a plugin that's already protecting the cluster.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="visual-summary">
                <div class="diagram-title">📊 Chapter 24 Visual Summary — Admission Control at a Glance</div>
                <div class="card-grid cols-3">
                    <div class="info-card">
                        <div class="card-icon-lg">🚪</div>
                        <h5>Built-in Plugins (24.1)</h5>
                        <p><strong>~30 plugins, 8 critical for CKS.</strong> Plugin chain runs mutating first (sequential), validating second (parallel). Configured via <code>--enable-admission-plugins</code> on API server. <strong>Always keep existing plugins when adding new ones.</strong></p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="info-card">
                        <div class="card-icon-lg">🪝</div>
                        <h5>Webhooks (24.2)</h5>
                        <p><strong>Mutating: sequential. Validating: parallel.</strong> TLS certs require CN matching Service DNS. <code>failurePolicy: Fail</code> = secure but risky. <code>Ignore</code> = available but insecure. objectSelector for fine-grained matching.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="info-card">
                        <div class="card-icon-lg">📜</div>
                        <h5>OPA Gatekeeper (24.3)</h5>
                        <p><strong>Rego language. Logic programming paradigm.</strong> ConstraintTemplate defines logic, Constraint applies it with parameters. Audit mode for safe rollout. Rego reusable across K8s, Terraform, CI/CD.</p>
