            <section class="section-block" id="s25-4">
                <h3 class="section-h">25.4 conftest — Testing YAML with OPA Rego Policies</h3>
                <p><strong>conftest</strong> tests structured configuration data (YAML, JSON, HCL, TOML, Dockerfiles) against policies written in <strong>OPA Rego</strong> — the same language used by OPA Gatekeeper (Ch24). Unlike kube-linter (fixed built-in checks) and kubesec (fixed scoring algorithm), conftest lets you define <strong>your own policies</strong>. This is the ultimate flexibility: enforce your organization's specific security standards, naming conventions, labeling requirements, and resource structure rules.</p>

                <h4>conftest vs OPA Gatekeeper — Same Language, Different Stage</h4>
                <div class="comparison-table">
                    <table>
                        <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>conftest (Ch25)</th><th>OPA Gatekeeper (Ch24)</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td><strong>When</strong></td><td>Pre-deployment (CI/CD, CLI, IDE)</td><td>Deployment time (API server admission)</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Input</strong></td><td>Static YAML/JSON files on disk</td><td>Live AdmissionReview API requests</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Language</strong></td><td>Rego (identical syntax)</td><td>Rego (identical syntax)</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Can test non-K8s</strong></td><td>✅ Dockerfiles, Terraform, HCL, TOML, JSON</td><td>❌ Kubernetes only</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Blocking</strong></td><td>Blocks CI/CD (non-zero exit code)</td><td>Blocks API request (403 Forbidden)</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Policy input path</strong></td><td><code>input.spec.template.spec.containers[_]</code></td><td><code>input.review.object.spec.containers[_]</code></td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>

                <h4>Fixture-Based Testing Pattern — Test Policies with Expected Results</h4>
                <div class="diagram-container">
                    <div class="diagram-title">conftest Fixture Testing — Policy + Test Fixtures + Expected Results</div>
<pre>
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │                    FIXTURE-BASED TESTING                               │
  │                                                                       │
  │  Directory structure:                                                 │
  │  policies/                                                            │
  │  ├── security.rego          ← Policy rules to test                    │
  │  ├── security_test.rego     ← Test assertions                         │
  │  └── fixtures/                                                        │
  │      ├── good-pod.yaml      ← Should PASS all policies               │
  │      └── bad-pod.yaml       ← Should FAIL specific policies           │
  │                                                                       │
  │  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │
  │  │  # policies/security_test.rego                                │    │
  │  │                                                                │    │
  │  │  package main                                                 │    │
  │  │                                                                │    │
  │  │  # Test: good-pod.yaml should have 0 deny results             │    │
  │  │  test_good_pod_has_no_violations {                            │    │
  │  │      count(deny) == 0 with input as yaml_unmarshal(           │    │
  │  │          file("fixtures/good-pod.yaml")                       │    │
  │  │      )                                                         │    │
  │  │  }                                                             │    │
  │  │                                                                │    │
  │  │  # Test: bad-pod.yaml should have at least 1 deny result      │    │
  │  │  test_bad_pod_has_violations {                                │    │
  │  │      count(deny) > 0 with input as yaml_unmarshal(            │    │
  │  │          file("fixtures/bad-pod.yaml")                        │    │
  │  │      )                                                         │    │
  │  │  }                                                             │    │
  │  │                                                                │    │
  │  │  # Run tests: conftest verify --policy policies/              │    │
  │  │  # Output: 2 tests passed, 0 tests failed                     │    │
  │  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘    │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
</pre>
                </div>

                <h4>Rego Policies for conftest — Security + Data + Warnings</h4>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header">
                        <span class="code-lang">Rego — policy/security.rego — Deny, warn, and data rules for easypj</span>
                    </div>
                    <pre><code class="language-rego">package main

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DENY RULES: Block the CI/CD pipeline (exit code 1)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

deny[msg] {
    container := input.spec.template.spec.containers[_]
    not container.securityContext
    msg := sprintf("container '%v' missing securityContext", [container.name])
}

deny[msg] {
    container := input.spec.template.spec.containers[_]
    container.securityContext.runAsUser == 0
    msg := sprintf("container '%v' running as root (UID 0)", [container.name])
}

deny[msg] {
    input.spec.template.spec.hostNetwork == true
    msg := "hostNetwork is not allowed"
}

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# WARN RULES: Show warnings but DON'T block (exit code 0)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

warn[msg] {
    container := input.spec.template.spec.containers[_]
    not container.resources.limits.cpu
    msg := sprintf("container '%v' missing CPU limit (recommended)", [container.name])
}

warn[msg] {
    container := input.spec.template.spec.containers[_]
    endswith(container.image, ":latest")
    msg := sprintf("container '%v' uses mutable ':latest' tag", [container.name])
}

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DATA RULES: Extract information (always runs, informational)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

images[image] {
    container := input.spec.template.spec.containers[_]
    image := container.image
}

container_count := count(input.spec.template.spec.containers)</code></pre>
