            <section class="section-block" id="s25-5">
                <h3 class="section-h">25.5 Integrating Static Analysis into easypj CI/CD — The Complete Security Gate</h3>
                <p>Each tool alone is useful. But together, they form a <strong>layered security gate</strong> that catches different classes of problems at different stages. The goal: <strong>no insecure manifest ever reaches the cluster.</strong> The pipeline starts at the developer's machine (pre-commit hooks), continues through PR review (CI checks), and culminates in image signing before deployment.</p>

                <h4>Developer Workflow — Pre-Commit Hooks for All Three Tools</h4>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header">
                        <span class="code-lang">YAML — .pre-commit-config.yaml — Run all three static analysis tools before git commit</span>
                    </div>
                    <pre><code class="language-yaml"># .pre-commit-config.yaml
# Install: pip install pre-commit && pre-commit install
# Now EVERY git commit runs these checks. Blocked if any fail.
repos:
- repo: local
  hooks:
  # ── kube-linter: Built-in K8s checks ──
  - id: kube-linter
    name: kube-linter (K8s security checks)
    entry: kube-linter lint
    language: system
    files: ^k8s/.*\.(yaml|yml)$
    pass_filenames: false
    args: ['k8s/']

  # ── kubesec: Security score threshold ──
  - id: kubesec
    name: kubesec (security scoring)
    entry: bash -c
    language: system
    files: ^k8s/.*\.(yaml|yml)$
    args:
    - |
      for f in k8s/*.yaml; do
        SCORE=$(kubesec scan "$f" | jq -r '.[0].score')
        if [ "$SCORE" -lt 4 ]; then
          echo "❌ $f scored $SCORE (needs ≥4)" && exit 1
        fi
      done

  # ── conftest: Custom Rego policies ──
  - id: conftest
    name: conftest (custom Rego policies)
    entry: conftest test --policy policies/
    language: system
    files: ^k8s/.*\.(yaml|yml)$
    pass_filenames: false
    args: ['k8s/']</code></pre>
