        <article class="chapter" id="ch26">
            <div class="chapter-intro">
            <h2 class="chapter-title">Chapter 26 · Image Signing — Cosign and Sigstore</h2>
            <p class="chapter-lead">You've built easypj:v2. Trivy says zero CRITICAL CVEs. kubesec scores it 8/10. kube-linter gives it a clean bill. You push it to your private registry. But here's the terrifying question: <strong>how does your Kubernetes cluster KNOW that the image in the registry is actually YOUR image?</strong> An attacker who compromises your registry credentials could push a malicious image with the exact same tag — and your cluster would pull it without hesitation. This is where <strong>image signing</strong> comes in: cryptographic proof, verified at admission time, that the image was built by you and only you. <strong>Cosign</strong> (part of the CNCF-backed Sigstore project) signs container images with digital signatures stored alongside the image in the registry. <strong>Kyverno</strong> verifies those signatures before allowing pods to run. Together, they close the supply chain's final gap: <strong>proving that what you built is what you deploy.</strong></p>
                <div class="chapter-meta">
                    <span class="meta-tag">🟡 Intermediate</span>
                    <span class="meta-tag">⏱️ ~2 hours</span>
                    <span class="meta-tag">✍️ Image Signing</span>
                    <span class="meta-tag">📦 Supply Chain</span>
                </div>
            </div><!-- /chapter-intro -->

            <div class="learning-objectives">
                <h4>🎯 What You'll Learn — Core-Level Mastery</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>✅ <strong>Cryptographic foundations:</strong> How ECDSA digital signatures work, why digest-based signing is essential, and the in-toto attestation framework</li>
                    <li>✅ <strong>Cosign key-based signing:</strong> Key generation with password protection, signing and verifying, key rotation strategies, multi-signer workflows</li>
