            <section class="section-block" id="s27-5">
                <h3 class="section-h">27.5 Supply Chain CI/CD Integration — Artifact Repository Security</h3>
                <p>The CKS curriculum requires you to <strong>understand your supply chain including CI/CD and artifact repositories</strong>. An artifact repository (like Harbor, Artifactory, ECR, GAR, ACR) is the bridge between your CI pipeline and your Kubernetes cluster. Securing it is as critical as securing the cluster itself:</p>
                <div class="diagram-container"><div class="diagram-title">Artifact Repository Security — Controls at Each Stage</div><pre>
  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  CI/CD PIPELINE                     ARTIFACT REPOSITORY              │
  │  ─────────────                      ───────────────────              │
  │                                                                      │
  │  1. git push ──→ 2. Build ──→ 3. Scan ──→ 4. Sign ──→ 5. Push     │
