                <h3 class="section-h">30.5 Incident Response Communication &amp; Post-Mortem</h3>
                <p>Technical response is half the battle. Communication and learning close the loop. Every incident should produce: a <strong>timeline</strong>, a <strong>root cause analysis</strong>, and <strong>prevention measures</strong>.</p>

                <h4>Post-Incident Actions — What to Do After the Attack Is Contained</h4>
                <div class="process-steps">
                    <div class="step"><span class="step-number">1</span><strong>Write the timeline</strong><p>Document every event with timestamps from audit logs and Falco alerts. This is your incident report.</p></div>
                    <div class="step"><span class="step-number">2</span><strong>Root cause analysis</strong><p>How did the attacker get in? Stolen SA token? Unpatched CVE? Misconfigured RBAC? Find and fix the root cause.</p></div>
