            <div class="chapter-intro">
            <h2 class="chapter-title">Chapter 32 · Compliance and Continuous Security Monitoring</h2>
            <p class="chapter-lead">Hardening a Kubernetes cluster is not a one-time task. <strong>New CVEs are published every day.</strong> Your perfectly-hardened easypj cluster today could have a CRITICAL vulnerability tomorrow. Configuration drifts when someone manually tweaks a NetworkPolicy or RBAC rule. <strong>Continuous security monitoring</strong> is the difference between catching a vulnerability in hours vs. discovering it months later after a breach. This chapter covers the detection &amp; alerting layer: Trivy Operator for continuous image scanning, kube-bench scheduled checks for configuration drift, OPA/Gatekeeper audit mode for policy compliance, and Prometheus/Grafana dashboards for security SLIs. <strong>This is your cluster's immune system — constantly scanning, detecting anomalies, and alerting before attackers exploit them.</strong></p>
                <div class="chapter-meta">
                    <span class="meta-tag">🟡 Intermediate</span>
                    <span class="meta-tag">⏱️ ~45 minutes</span>
