            <section class="section-block" id="s32-1">
                <h3 class="section-h">32.1 Continuous Security Scanning — Keeping the Cluster Clean</h3>
                <p>One-time image scanning at CI/CD is necessary but <strong>insufficient</strong>. A CVE discovered <em>after</em> your image was built leaves already-deployed pods vulnerable. <strong>Trivy Operator</strong> (by Aqua Security) runs <em>inside</em> the cluster, continuously scanning all container images across all namespaces and producing <strong>VulnerabilityReport CRDs</strong>. When a new CVE is published, Trivy Operator re-scans and updates the reports — you get alerted without waiting for the next release cycle.</p>

                <div class="info-box tip">
                    <div class="info-box-title">💡 Why Continuous Scanning?</div>
                    <p>A CVE like <code>CVE-2024-21626</code> (runc container breakout) is discovered <em>after</em> images are built. Without continuous scanning, your running pods are vulnerable for weeks before the next CI build. Trivy Operator found 1,247 clusters running vulnerable runc within 24 hours of the CVE disclosure.</p>
                </div>

