                <h4>Trivy Operator CRDs — The Full Vulnerability Data Model</h4>
                <p>Trivy Operator creates <strong>five types of CRDs</strong> in your cluster. Each one represents a different security dimension:</p>
                <div class="card-grid cols-3">
                    <div class="info-card"><div class="card-icon-lg">🔴</div><h5>VulnerabilityReport</h5><p>Per-workload CVE scan. Maps every CVE to the pod's container images. <strong>This is the primary CRD for continuous scanning.</strong> Updated on schedule + on pod changes.</p><p><small>Namespaced — one per ReplicaSet/Deployment/StatefulSet</small></p></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><div class="card-icon-lg">⚙️</div><h5>ConfigAuditReport</h5><p>Checks Kubernetes workload manifests for misconfigurations: privileged containers, writable filesystems, missing resource limits, hostPath mounts. <strong>Like kubesec but continuous.</strong></p><p><small>Namespaced — one per workload</small></p></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><div class="card-icon-lg">🔑</div><h5>ExposedSecretReport</h5><p>Scans for exposed passwords, API keys, tokens in container images and ConfigMaps. <strong>Hardcoded secrets are a top OWASP risk.</strong></p><p><small>Namespaced — one per workload</small></p></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><div class="card-icon-lg">📊</div><h5>ClusterComplianceReport</h5><p>Aggregates findings per namespace or cluster-wide against CIS/NSA/PSS benchmarks. Shows pass/fail counts per control group.</p><p><small>Cluster-scoped — summary across namespaces</small></p></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><div class="card-icon-lg">📦</div><h5>SbomReport</h5><p>Software Bill of Materials — lists every package in your container image. <strong>Critical for supply chain transparency</strong> and identifying affected images when a new CVE drops.</p><p><small>Namespaced — one per workload</small></p></div>
