        <article class="chapter" id="ch33">
            <div class="chapter-intro">
            <h2 class="chapter-title">Chapter 33 · Complete Security Hardening of easypj/jobpost</h2>
            <p class="chapter-lead">You've learned the theory. Now let's <strong>apply every CKS control</strong> to a real application. <strong>easypj/jobpost</strong> is a Django-based job board — 5 models (JobPost, Author, Location, Skills, User), PostgreSQL database, Redis cache. Right now it runs with <strong>zero security hardening</strong>: pods run as root, no NetworkPolicies, secrets in plaintext, no image scanning. This chapter takes you from a <strong>kubesec score of 2/10</strong> to a CKS-exam-ready <strong>8/10</strong> — applying RBAC, PSS, Seccomp, AppArmor, read-only filesystems, NetworkPolicy, encryption at rest, Falco monitoring, and image supply chain security. <strong>Every code block in this chapter is production-ready — copy, adapt, deploy.</strong></p>
            <div class="chapter-meta">
                <span class="meta-tag">🔴 Advanced</span>
                <span class="meta-tag">⏱️ ~2 hours</span>
                <span class="meta-tag">🏗️ Hands-On</span>
                <span class="meta-tag">🛡️ Full Stack Security</span>
            </div>
            </div><!-- /chapter-intro -->

            <div class="learning-objectives">
                <h4>🎯 What You'll Learn — Core-Level Mastery</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>✅ <strong>Assess baseline security:</strong> Run kube-bench, kubesec, and Trivy on an unsecured cluster to quantify the starting risk</li>
                    <li>✅ <strong>Harden the image supply chain:</strong> Multi-stage Dockerfile, Trivy CI scan, cosign signing, Kyverno verification — end-to-end</li>
                    <li>✅ <strong>Apply defense-in-depth pod security:</strong> Non-root user, read-only FS, drop ALL capabilities, Seccomp RuntimeDefault, custom AppArmor profile</li>
                    <li>✅ <strong>Enforce admission control:</strong> PSS Restricted labels, OPA Gatekeeper image registry policy, Kyverno verifyImages for cosign signatures</li>
                    <li>✅ <strong>Least-privilege RBAC:</strong> Dedicated ServiceAccounts, disabled automount, minimal Roles/RoleBindings per workload</li>
