            <section class="section-block" id="s33-2">
                <h3 class="section-h">33.2 Step 1 — Secure the Image and Supply Chain</h3>
                <p>The first line of defense is the <strong>container image itself</strong>. A hardened image is small (minimal attack surface), free of CRITICAL CVEs, signed for integrity verification, and runs as a non-root user by design. This section walks through the complete supply chain: build → scan → sign → verify.</p>

                <h4>Hardened Multi-Stage Dockerfile for easypj</h4>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header">
                        <span class="code-lang">Dockerfile — Multi-stage build: compile in full image, run in minimal</span>
                    </div>
                    <pre><code class="language-dockerfile"># ============================================
# STAGE 1: BUILDER — Compile Python dependencies
# ============================================
FROM python:3.12-slim-bookworm AS builder

# Install build dependencies ONLY (removed from final image)
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
    build-essential \
    libpq-dev \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

# Create non-root user EARLY (security best practice)
RUN groupadd -r easypj && useradd -r -g easypj -m -s /bin/bash easypj

WORKDIR /app

# Copy ONLY requirements first (leverage Docker layer caching)
COPY requirements.txt .

# Install into a VIRTUAL ENVIRONMENT (isolated from system Python)
RUN python -m venv /opt/venv && \
    /opt/venv/bin/pip install --no-cache-dir --upgrade pip setuptools && \
    /opt/venv/bin/pip install --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt && \
    /opt/venv/bin/pip install --no-cache-dir \
      gunicorn==22.0.0 \
      psycopg2-binary==2.9.9 \
      django-storages==1.14.4

# ============================================
# STAGE 2: RUNTIME — Minimal production image
# ============================================
FROM python:3.12-slim-bookworm

# Install ONLY runtime libraries (NOT build tools!)
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
    libpq5 \
    curl \
    ca-certificates \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/* \
    && apt-get clean

# Create the SAME non-root user (UID/GID must match or files owned by nobody)
RUN groupadd -r easypj && useradd -r -g easypj -m -s /bin/bash easypj

# Copy virtual environment from builder (NO build tools in final image!)
COPY --from=builder /opt/venv /opt/venv

# Set environment variables
ENV PATH="/opt/venv/bin:$PATH" \
    PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 \
    PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 \
    PYTHONHASHSEED=random \
    DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE=easypj.settings

WORKDIR /app

# Copy application code AFTER dependencies (layer caching optimization)
COPY --chown=easypj:easypj . .

# Create writable directories (these will be mounted as emptyDir later)
RUN mkdir -p /app/staticfiles /app/media /tmp/app && \
    chown -R easypj:easypj /app/staticfiles /app/media /tmp/app

# Switch to non-root user — ALL processes run as UID 1000 from here
USER easypj

# Collect static files during build (immutable assets)
RUN python manage.py collectstatic --noinput

EXPOSE 8000

# Health check — Kubernetes uses this to determine pod readiness
HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=5s --start-period=15s --retries=3 \
    CMD curl -f http://localhost:8000/healthz/ || exit 1

# Run Gunicorn with optimized settings for production
CMD ["gunicorn", "easypj.wsgi:application", \
     "--bind", "0.0.0.0:8000", \
     "--workers", "3", \
     "--threads", "2", \
     "--timeout", "60", \
     "--max-requests", "1000", \
     "--max-requests-jitter", "100", \
     "--access-logfile", "-", \
     "--error-logfile", "-"]</code></pre>
                </div>

