                <h4>Cosign Keyless Signing — How It Works Under the Hood</h4>
                <div class="process-steps">
                    <div class="step"><span class="step-number">1</span><strong>OIDC Token Issued</strong><p>GitHub Actions requests an OIDC token from <code>token.actions.githubusercontent.com</code>. The token contains claims: <code>subject</code> (repo + workflow ref), <code>issuer</code> (GitHub), <code>repository</code>. No long-lived key needed!</p></div>
                    <div class="step"><span class="step-number">2</span><strong>Ephemeral Key Pair Generated</strong><p>Cosign generates a short-lived key pair. The private key signs the image digest. The public key is embedded in a certificate.</p></div>
                    <div class="step"><span class="step-number">3</span><strong>Certificate Transparency Log</strong><p>The certificate is uploaded to <strong>Rekor</strong> (Sigstore's transparency log). Anyone can verify: "This image was signed by GitHub Actions workflow X at time Y."</p></div>
                    <div class="step"><span class="step-number">4</span><strong>Signature Stored in Registry</strong><p>The signature is pushed to the OCI registry alongside the image. It's stored as a separate artifact, tagged <code>sha256-XXXX.sig</code>.</p></div>
                </div>

                <h4>Verifying Image Signatures Manually</h4>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header">
                        <span class="code-lang">Bash — Manually verify a cosign-signed image</span>
                    </div>
                    <pre><code class="language-bash"># Verify the image was signed by OUR GitHub Actions workflow
cosign verify \
  --certificate-identity "https://github.com/Anihs-Canvas/DEV-DOCs/.github/workflows/build.yml@refs/heads/main" \
  --certificate-oidc-issuer "https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com" \
  ghcr.io/anihs-canvas/easypj@sha256:abc123...

# Output:
# Verification for ghcr.io/anihs-canvas/easypj@sha256:abc123... --
# The following checks were performed on each of these signatures:
#   ✅ The specified identity was matched
#   ✅ The specified OIDC issuer was matched
#   ✅ The signature was verified against the specified certificate
#   ✅ The certificate was verified against the Fulcio root
#   ✅ The signature was stored in Rekor transparency log

# ALSO verify the SBOM was signed
cosign verify-attestation \
  --type cyclonedx \
  --certificate-identity "https://github.com/Anihs-Canvas/DEV-DOCs/.github/workflows/build.yml@refs/heads/main" \
  --certificate-oidc-issuer "https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com" \
  ghcr.io/anihs-canvas/easypj@sha256:abc123...</code></pre>
                </div>
