                <h4>Automating the Incident Response Playbook</h4>
                <p>Manual response takes 40 minutes. Automation can reduce this to <strong>under 5 minutes</strong>. Here's a script that executes the entire containment + forensics workflow:</p>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header">
                        <span class="code-lang">Bash — Automated incident response script (triggered by Falco alert webhook)</span>
                    </div>
                    <pre><code class="language-bash">#!/bin/bash
# auto-ir.sh — Automated Incident Response for easypj
# Trigger: Falco alert "Shell in easypj container" webhook

set -euo pipefail

POD_NAME="${1:-}"
NAMESPACE="${2:-easypj-prod}"

if [ -z "$POD_NAME" ]; then
  echo "Usage: $0 <pod-name> [namespace]"
  exit 1
fi

TIMESTAMP=$(date -u +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S)
CASE_DIR="/var/forensics/${TIMESTAMP}-${POD_NAME}"
mkdir -p "$CASE_DIR"

echo "🚨 AUTO-IR: Isolating pod $POD_NAME in namespace $NAMESPACE"

# Phase 1: CONTAIN (automated)
echo "  [1/5] Isolating pod..."
kubectl label pod "$POD_NAME" -n "$NAMESPACE" app- --overwrite 2>/dev/null || true

cat &lt;&lt;EOF | kubectl apply -f -
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: quarantine-${POD_NAME}
  namespace: ${NAMESPACE}
spec:
  podSelector:
    matchLabels:
      pod-name: ${POD_NAME}
  policyTypes: [Ingress, Egress]
EOF

echo "  [2/5] Capturing forensics..."
kubectl get pod "$POD_NAME" -n "$NAMESPACE" -o yaml > "$CASE_DIR/pod-spec.yaml"
kubectl exec "$POD_NAME" -n "$NAMESPACE" -- env > "$CASE_DIR/env.txt" 2>/dev/null || true
kubectl exec "$POD_NAME" -n "$NAMESPACE" -- ps auxf > "$CASE_DIR/processes.txt" 2>/dev/null || true
kubectl exec "$POD_NAME" -n "$NAMESPACE" -- ss -tunap > "$CASE_DIR/network.txt" 2>/dev/null || true
kubectl logs "$POD_NAME" -n "$NAMESPACE" --tail=1000 > "$CASE_DIR/logs.txt" 2>/dev/null || true

echo "  [3/5] Hashing evidence..."
cd "$CASE_DIR" && sha256sum * > chain-of-custody.sha256

echo "  [4/5] Sending alerts..."
# Send to Slack
curl -s -X POST -H 'Content-type: application/json' \
  --data "{\"text\":\"🚨 AUTO-IR: Pod $POD_NAME in $NAMESPACE isolated. Forensics saved to $CASE_DIR\"}" \
  "$SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL" || true

echo "  [5/5] Rotating credentials..."
kubectl -n "$NAMESPACE" delete secret easypj-secrets 2>/dev/null || true
kubectl -n "$NAMESPACE" create secret generic easypj-secrets \
  --from-literal=django-secret-key="$(openssl rand -base64 48)" \
  --from-literal=db-password="$(openssl rand -base64 32)" \
  --from-literal=redis-password="$(openssl rand -base64 24)"

echo "✅ AUTO-IR COMPLETE: $POD_NAME isolated, forensics at $CASE_DIR, credentials rotated"
echo "   Manual steps remaining: (1) Review forensics, (2) Fix vulnerability, (3) Rebuild + redeploy"</code></pre>
