            <section class="section-block" id="s35-1">
                <h3 class="section-h">35.1 GitOps Security — Why Security Should Live in Git</h3>
                <p>GitOps applies the same principles that revolutionized application deployment to <strong>security configuration</strong>. Instead of running <code>kubectl apply -f network-policy.yaml</code> from someone's laptop, every security manifest lives in a Git repository. Changes go through PR review, automated validation, and are deployed by an operator (ArgoCD) that continuously reconciles the desired state in Git with the actual state in the cluster.</p>

                <h4>The GitOps Security Loop — PR → Review → Deploy → Detect Drift</h4>
                <div class="diagram-container">
                    <div class="diagram-title">GitOps Security Workflow for easypj</div>
<pre>
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │                        GIT REPOSITORY                                 │
  │  easypj-security/                                                    │
  │  ├── rbac/                     # All RBAC manifests                   │
  │  ├── network-policies/         # All NetworkPolicies                  │
  │  ├── pss-labels/               # Namespace PSS enforcement labels     │
  │  ├── gatekeeper/               # ConstraintTemplates + Constraints    │
  │  ├── kyverno/                  # ClusterPolicies + verifyImages       │
  │  ├── falco/                    # Custom Falco rules                   │
  │  ├── audit/                    # Audit policy                         │
  │  └── argocd/                   # ArgoCD Application definitions       │
  └──────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                     │
                     │ ① Developer creates PR to change a NetworkPolicy
                     ▼
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │                     GITHUB ACTIONS (CI)                               │
  │  PR Checks:                                                          │
  │    ✅ YAML lint (yamllint)                                           │
  │    ✅ kube-linter (best practices)                                   │
  │    ✅ kubesec (security scoring)                                     │
  │    ✅ conftest (Rego policy validation)                              │
  │    ✅ kubectl --dry-run=server (API server validation)               │
  │  All checks PASS → PR can be merged                                  │
  └──────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                     │
                     │ ② Security team reviews + approves PR
                     ▼
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │                     ARGOCD (CD)                                       │
  │  Watches Git repo every 3 minutes:                                   │
  │    → Detects new commit on main branch                              │
  │    → Syncs: applies changed manifests to cluster                    │
  │    → Prunes: removes resources deleted from Git                     │
  │    → Reports: "Synced" or "OutOfSync" in ArgoCD UI                  │
  └──────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                     │
                     │ ③ ArgoCD applies NetworkPolicy to cluster
                     ▼
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │                     KUBERNETES CLUSTER                                │
  │  Desired state = Git. Actual state = cluster.                        │
  │  ArgoCD detects drift: if someone runs kubectl edit and changes     │
  │  the policy, ArgoCD DETECTS the deviation and AUTO-CORRECTS it.     │
  │  Drift alert is logged + optionally sent to Slack.                  │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
</pre>
                </div>

                <h4>Why GitOps Beats Manual Security Management</h4>
                <div class="comparison-table">
                    <table>
                        <thead><tr><th>Concern</th><th>Manual (kubectl apply)</th><th>GitOps (ArgoCD)</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td><strong>Audit trail</strong></td><td>❌ Who changed what? Check <code>kubectl get events</code> — often expired.</td><td>✅ Every change is a Git commit: author, timestamp, diff, PR review, approval chain.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Review process</strong></td><td>❌ No mandatory review. One person can accidentally delete a NetworkPolicy.</td><td>✅ PR requires approval from security team. Branch protection prevents direct pushes to main.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Drift detection</strong></td><td>❌ Manual changes go undetected. Someone <code>kubectl edit</code> and it's silently different.</td><td>✅ ArgoCD compares every 3 minutes. Drift is detected and auto-corrected (or alerted).</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Disaster recovery</strong></td><td>❌ Cluster destroyed → security config lost. Hope someone has a local copy.</td><td>✅ <code>git clone</code> + ArgoCD → entire security posture restored in minutes.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Multi-cluster consistency</strong></td><td>❌ Staging and production diverge. "It worked in staging!"</td><td>✅ Same Git repo deploys to staging and production. Only difference is cluster-specific config.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><strong>Rollback</strong></td><td>❌ <code>kubectl apply -f old-version.yaml</code> — if you can find it.</td><td>✅ <code>git revert</code> the bad commit. ArgoCD syncs the revert automatically.</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>

                <h4>ArgoCD Application — Deploy Security Policies from Git</h4>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header">
                        <span class="code-lang">YAML — ArgoCD Application: Sync easypj security policies from Git to cluster</span>
                    </div>
                    <pre><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
kind: Application
metadata:
  name: easypj-security-policies
  namespace: argocd
  finalizers:
  - resources-finalizer.argocd.argoproj.io   # Clean up on deletion
spec:
  project: default
  source:
    repoURL: https://github.com/Anihs-Canvas/easypj-security.git
    targetRevision: main                       # Track main branch
    path: .                                    # Root of the repo
    directory:
      recurse: true                            # Apply all subdirectories
      jsonnet: {}
  destination:
    server: https://kubernetes.default.svc
    namespace: argocd                          # Policies deployed cluster-wide
  syncPolicy:
    automated:
      prune: true                              # Delete resources removed from Git
      selfHeal: true                           # Auto-correct manual drift
      allowEmpty: false
    syncOptions:
    - Validate=true                            # Validate manifests before applying
    - CreateNamespace=true
    - PrunePropagationPolicy=foreground
    retry:
      limit: 5
      backoff:
        duration: 5s
        factor: 2
        maxDuration: 3m</code></pre>
