            <span class="ch-jump" id="ch35-gotchas"></span>
            <div class="cka-gotcha">
                <h5>⚠️ Common Gotchas &amp; Misconceptions</h5>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>"Secrets in Git are fine if the repo is private."</strong> Even encrypted, secrets in Git are risky — history persists, access lists grow, and forks/clones leak. Use External Secrets Operator (Ch 20) or SealedSecrets instead. Never commit plaintext secrets; the CKS exam will flag this as a critical violation.</li>
                    <li><strong>"ArgoCD should just get cluster-admin so it never fails to sync."</strong> The ArgoCD ServiceAccount needs cluster-wide READ access to detect drift, but write access should be scoped to only the namespaces it manages — never cluster-admin. Over-granting ArgoCD turns a GitOps compromise into a full cluster compromise.</li>
                    <li><strong>"selfHeal and automated sync are the same thing."</strong> Automated sync applies new Git commits; it does NOT revert manual cluster edits by itself. Only <code>selfHeal: true</code> continuously reverts drift, including changes never committed to Git.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

