                    <div class="info-card"><div class="card-icon-lg">🚫</div><h5>Reading ALL tasks before starting ANY</h5><p>Some candidates spend 15+ minutes reading every task in detail. You don't need to understand every task upfront. Scan for 30 seconds each — just enough to classify difficulty. Start solving immediately.</p></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><div class="card-icon-lg">🚫</div><h5>Perfecting one answer for 20 minutes</h5><p>A task is worth the same whether you spend 3 minutes or 20 minutes on it. If you're 8 minutes in and not close to done, SKIP. Come back in Pass 3. A partial solution may earn partial credit.</p></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><div class="card-icon-lg">🚫</div><h5>Not using the documentation</h5><p>The Kubernetes docs are YOUR notes. You don't need to memorize YAML syntax — copy from the docs. Search for "NetworkPolicy" → copy the example → modify it. This is faster than writing from scratch and less error-prone.</p></div>
