            <section class="section-block" id="s36-4">
                <h3 class="section-h">36.4 File Locations You Must Know (No Internet Search Needed)</h3>
                <p>In the CKS exam, searching the Kubernetes documentation for file paths wastes precious minutes. These paths appear in nearly every exam task. <strong>Memorize them.</strong> Write them on a piece of paper and review them 5 minutes before your exam starts (during the check-in process, you'll have a few minutes while the proctor verifies your ID).</p>

                <h4>Critical File Paths — Categorized by Component</h4>
                <div class="comparison-table">
                    <table>
                        <thead><tr><th>File / Directory</th><th>Component</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Common Task</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td><code>/etc/kubernetes/manifests/</code></td><td>kubelet</td><td>Static pod manifests directory. Any YAML here is automatically run as a static pod.</td><td>Edit API server, controller-manager, scheduler, or etcd configuration</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-apiserver.yaml</code></td><td>API Server</td><td>API server static pod manifest. Add flags here to configure encryption, audit, admission plugins.</td><td>Enable encryption at rest, configure audit policy, disable anonymous auth</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-controller-manager.yaml</code></td><td>Controller Manager</td><td>Controller manager static pod manifest.</td><td>Configure ServiceAccount token signing, enable/disable controllers</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/etc/kubernetes/manifests/etcd.yaml</code></td><td>etcd</td><td>etcd static pod manifest. Configure TLS, peer URLs, data directory.</td><td>Enable TLS for etcd, change data directory</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/var/lib/kubelet/config.yaml</code></td><td>kubelet</td><td>Kubelet configuration file (YAML). Contains authentication, authorization, cgroup driver settings.</td><td>Disable anonymous auth, enable webhook authorization, set Seccomp default</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/etc/kubernetes/pki/</code></td><td>PKI</td><td>Cluster certificate authority and key files.</td><td>Inspect certificate expiration, rotate certificates</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/</code></td><td>etcd PKI</td><td>etcd-specific certificates and keys.</td><td>Configure etcd TLS, verify peer certificates</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/var/lib/etcd/</code></td><td>etcd</td><td>etcd data directory. Contains the actual key-value store data.</td><td>Backup, restore, check data size</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/etc/kubernetes/audit-policy.yaml</code></td><td>API Server</td><td>Audit policy file. Defines WHAT to log and at what detail level.</td><td>Create or modify audit policy, enable audit logging</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/etc/falco/falco.yaml</code></td><td>Falco</td><td>Falco main configuration file. Output channels, rules files, engine settings.</td><td>Change output format, enable/disable rules, configure alerting</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/etc/falco/falco_rules.yaml</code></td><td>Falco</td><td>Default Falco rules. Shipped with Falco installation.</td><td>View default rules for reference when writing custom rules</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/etc/falco/falco_rules.local.yaml</code></td><td>Falco</td><td>LOCAL custom rules file. Add your custom rules here (never edit the default file).</td><td>Write custom Falco rules for specific applications</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/var/lib/kubelet/seccomp/</code></td><td>kubelet</td><td>Directory for local Seccomp profiles. Place custom JSON profiles here.</td><td>Create and apply custom Seccomp profiles</td></tr>
                            <tr><td><code>/etc/apparmor.d/</code></td><td>AppArmor</td><td>AppArmor profile directory. Place custom AppArmor profiles here.</td><td>Load and apply custom AppArmor profiles to pods</td></tr>
