                <h4>Memorization Strategy — How to Remember These Paths</h4>
                <div class="card-grid cols-3">
                    <div class="info-card"><div class="card-icon-lg">🧠</div><h5>Group by Parent Directory</h5><p>Most paths live under 3 parents: <code>/etc/kubernetes/</code> (API server, PKI, audit), <code>/var/lib/kubelet/</code> (kubelet config, Seccomp), and <code>/etc/falco/</code> (Falco rules). Memorize the 3 parents first, then the specific files under each.</p></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><div class="card-icon-lg">📝</div><h5>Write Them Before Starting</h5><p>During the NDA/check-in screen (you have a few minutes), mentally recite these paths. As soon as the terminal appears, type them into the notepad: <code>/etc/kubernetes/manifests/</code>, <code>/var/lib/kubelet/config.yaml</code>, <code>/etc/falco/falco_rules.local.yaml</code>. Your future self will thank you.</p></div>
                    <div class="info-card"><div class="card-icon-lg">🔗</div><h5>Associate with Tasks</h5><p>Don't memorize in isolation. Link each path to a specific task: "If I need to enable encryption → edit <code>/etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-apiserver.yaml</code>". "If I need to write a custom Falco rule → edit <code>/etc/falco/falco_rules.local.yaml</code>". The association makes it stick.</p></div>
