                <h4>Task A: Disable Anonymous Auth on API Server, Verify</h4>
                <div class="scenario-box">
                    <div class="scenario-header"><span class="scenario-badge info">TASK</span><span class="scenario-title">Context: mk8s-cluster-2 | Time: 4 min | Points: 4</span></div>
                    <div class="scenario-steps">
                        <div class="scenario-step"><div class="step-marker">📋</div><div class="step-content"><strong>Objective:</strong> Disable anonymous authentication on the Kubernetes API server. Verify that anonymous requests are rejected.</div></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-lang">✅ Solution</span></div>
                    <pre><code class="language-bash"># Step 1: SSH to control plane node
ssh control-plane-1

# Step 2: Edit API server manifest
sudo vi /etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-apiserver.yaml
# Find: - --anonymous-auth=true  (or add if missing)
# Change to: - --anonymous-auth=false
# Save and exit

# Step 3: Wait for API server to restart (~30 seconds)
kubectl get pods -n kube-system | grep apiserver
# Should show a new pod with AGE of a few seconds

# Step 4: Verify — anonymous request should FAIL
kubectl get pods --as=system:anonymous
# Expected: Error from server (Forbidden): pods is forbidden: User "system:anonymous" cannot list

# Step 5: Verify authenticated request still works
kubectl get pods -n kube-system
# Should return pod list normally</code></pre>
