                <h4>Task A: Load AppArmor Profile and Apply to a Pod</h4>
                <div class="scenario-box">
                    <div class="scenario-header"><span class="scenario-badge info">TASK</span><span class="scenario-title">Context: mk8s-cluster-3 | Time: 8 min | Points: 6</span></div>
                    <div class="scenario-steps">
                        <div class="scenario-step"><div class="step-marker">📋</div><div class="step-content"><strong>Objective:</strong> Create a custom AppArmor profile that denies writing to /tmp. Load it on the node. Create a pod with this profile and verify writes to /tmp are blocked.</div></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-lang">✅ Solution</span></div>
                    <pre><code class="language-bash"># Step 1: SSH to worker node where pod will run
ssh worker-1

# Step 2: Create AppArmor profile
sudo tee /etc/apparmor.d/deny-tmp-write &lt;&lt;EOF
#include &lt;tunables/global&gt;
profile deny-tmp-write flags=(attach_disconnected) {
  #include &lt;abstractions/base&gt;
  /tmp/  r,
  /tmp/** r,
  deny /tmp/** w,
}
EOF

# Step 3: Load the profile
sudo apparmor_parser -r /etc/apparmor.d/deny-tmp-write
sudo aa-status | grep deny-tmp-write   # Verify loaded

# Step 4: Create pod with AppArmor annotation
cat &lt;&lt;EOF | kubectl apply -f -
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: apparmor-test
  annotations:
    container.apparmor.security.beta.kubernetes.io/test: localhost/deny-tmp-write
spec:
  containers:
  - name: test
    image: nginx
EOF

# Step 5: Verify — write to /tmp should FAIL
kubectl exec apparmor-test -- touch /tmp/test-file
# Expected: touch: cannot touch '/tmp/test-file': Permission denied</code></pre>
