                <h4>Task A: Configure Falco Audit Policy — Log Secret Reads</h4>
                <div class="scenario-box">
                    <div class="scenario-header"><span class="scenario-badge info">TASK</span><span class="scenario-title">Context: mk8s-cluster-6 | Time: 7 min | Points: 5</span></div>
                    <div class="scenario-steps">
                        <div class="scenario-step"><div class="step-marker">📋</div><div class="step-content"><strong>Objective:</strong> Edit the Kubernetes audit policy to log all Secret reads at Metadata level and pod exec at RequestResponse level. Enable the policy. Verify it works by reading a Secret and checking the audit log.</div></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-lang">✅ Solution</span></div>
                    <pre><code class="language-bash"># Step 1: Create/update audit policy
sudo tee /etc/kubernetes/audit-policy.yaml &lt;&lt;EOF
apiVersion: audit.k8s.io/v1
kind: Policy
rules:
- level: Metadata
  resources:
  - group: ""
    resources: ["secrets"]
- level: RequestResponse
  verbs: ["create"]
  resources:
  - group: ""
    resources: ["pods/exec"]
- level: None
  verbs: ["get", "list", "watch"]
  resources:
  - group: ""
    resources: ["pods", "services"]
EOF

# Step 2: Verify API server has audit flags
# (See Task 37.2B for full API server configuration)
sudo vi /etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-apiserver.yaml
# Ensure flags: --audit-policy-file, --audit-log-path

# Step 3: Test — create and read a secret
kubectl create secret generic falco-audit-test --from-literal=key=demo -n default
kubectl get secret falco-audit-test -n default -o yaml > /dev/null

# Step 4: Verify audit log
sudo cat /var/log/kubernetes/audit.log | jq 'select(.objectRef.resource=="secrets") | {verb, user: .user.username, secret: .objectRef.name}' | tail -5
# Should show the GET request for falco-audit-test</code></pre>
