            <section class="section-block" id="s38-1">
                <h3 class="section-h">38.1 One-Page CKS Domain Cheat Sheet</h3>
                <p>This is the ultimate reference. <strong>Every key command and file path</strong> organized by CKS exam domain. If you memorize nothing else, memorize this page:</p>

                <div class="diagram-container">
                    <div class="diagram-title">CKS Domain Cheat Sheet — Key Commands + Files Per Domain</div>
<pre>
  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │  DOMAIN 1: CLUSTER SETUP (10%)                                              │
  │  ───────────────────────────────                                             │
  │  kube-bench run --targets=master              # Run CIS benchmark           │
  │  vi /etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-apiserver.yaml  # Edit API server        │
  │  kubectl apply -f networkpolicy.yaml           # Apply NetworkPolicy        │
  │  kubectl create secret tls tls-secret \        # Create TLS secret          │
  │    --cert=tls.crt --key=tls.key                                              │
  │  openssl req -x509 -nodes -days 365 \          # Generate self-signed cert  │
  │    -newkey rsa:2048 -keyout tls.key -out tls.crt -subj "/CN=test"          │
  ├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  DOMAIN 2: CLUSTER HARDENING (15%)                                          │
  │  ───────────────────────────────────                                         │
  │  # API server hardening flags:                                              │
  │  --anonymous-auth=false --profiling=false                                   │
  │  --authorization-mode=Node,RBAC                                             │
  │  --audit-policy-file=/etc/kubernetes/audit/policy.yaml                     │
  │  --audit-log-path=/var/log/kubernetes/audit.log                            │
  │  --encryption-provider-config=/etc/kubernetes/encryption-config.yaml       │
  │                                                                             │
  │  kubectl create role r1 --verb=get,list --resource=pods -n ns              │
  │  kubectl create rolebinding rb1 --role=r1 --sa=ns:sa -n ns                 │
  │  kubectl auth can-i get pods --as=system:serviceaccount:ns:sa -n ns       │
  │  kubectl create sa mysa -n ns                                               │
  │  # Disable automount: spec.automountServiceAccountToken: false             │
  ├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  DOMAIN 3: SYSTEM HARDENING (15%)                                           │
  │  ────────────────────────────────                                            │
  │  aa-status | grep profile-name                   # Check AppArmor status    │
  │  apparmor_parser -r /etc/apparmor.d/profile      # Load AppArmor profile    │
  │  # Pod annotation: container.apparmor.security.beta.kubernetes.io/NAME     │
  │  # Pod securityContext: seccompProfile.type: RuntimeDefault                │
  │  cat /proc/PID/status | grep Seccomp             # Verify Seccomp active   │
  │  systemctl restart kubelet                        # Restart after config    │
  │  vi /var/lib/kubelet/config.yaml                 # Kubelet configuration    │
  │  systemctl stop <svc> && systemctl disable <svc>  # Remove services         │
  ├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  DOMAIN 4: MICROSERVICE VULNERABILITIES (20%)                               │
  │  ─────────────────────────────────────────────                               │
  │  kubectl label ns NAME pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce=restricted       │
  │  kubectl label ns NAME pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce-version=v1.30   │
  │  # Pod securityContext (7 fields):                                          │
  │  runAsNonRoot:true, runAsUser:1000, allowPrivilegeEscalation:false         │
  │  readOnlyRootFilesystem:true, capabilities.drop:[ALL]                      │
  │  seccompProfile.type:RuntimeDefault, AppArmor annotation                   │
  │                                                                             │
  │  # EncryptionConfiguration: /etc/kubernetes/encryption-config.yaml         │
  │  ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl get /registry/secrets/NS/NAME | hexdump -C         │
  ├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │  DOMAIN 5: SUPPLY CHAIN SECURITY (20%)                                      │
  │  ─────────────────────────────────────                                       │
  │  trivy image --severity CRITICAL,HIGH IMAGE:TAG    # Scan image             │
  │  trivy image --format json -o report.json IMAGE    # JSON output            │
  │  cosign generate-key-pair                           # Generate signing keys  │
  │  cosign sign --key cosign.key IMAGE@sha256:...     # Sign image             │
