                <h4>How to Use This Cheat Sheet During the Exam</h4>
                <div class="process-steps">
                    <div class="step"><span class="step-number">1</span><strong>Identify the domain</strong><p>Read the task description. Does it mention kube-bench? → Domain 1. API server flags? → Domain 2. AppArmor/Seccomp? → Domain 3. PSS or encryption? → Domain 4. Trivy/cosign? → Domain 5. Falco/audit? → Domain 6. This mental mapping takes 5 seconds and tells you which section to scan.</p></div>
                    <div class="step"><span class="step-number">2</span><strong>Scan the domain section</strong><p>Each domain lists 4-6 commands. 90% of exam tasks can be solved with just these commands. If the exact command isn't listed, the DOMAIN tells you which tool to search for in the Kubernetes docs.</p></div>
                    <div class="step"><span class="step-number">3</span><strong>Type — don't copy-paste</strong><p>The PSI browser doesn't allow copy-paste from the exam content to your terminal. Memorize the command patterns, not the exact syntax. For example: <code>kubectl create role NAME --verb=VERB --resource=RESOURCE -n NS</code> — the pattern is what matters.</p></div>
