            <section class="section-block" id="sa-1">
                <h3 class="section-h">A.1 Authentication and Authorization Commands</h3>
                <p>RBAC is the foundation of Kubernetes security. These commands create, inspect, and verify roles, bindings, and service accounts. <strong>You'll use these in 30%+ of CKS exam tasks.</strong></p>

                <h4>Service Account Management</h4>
                <div class="comparison-table">
                    <table>
                        <thead><tr><th style="width:8%;">⚡</th><th style="width:35%;">Command</th><th style="width:30%;">What It Does</th><th style="width:27%;">Example</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td>⚡</td><td><code>kubectl create sa &lt;name&gt; -n &lt;ns&gt;</code></td><td>Create a dedicated ServiceAccount</td><td><code>kubectl create sa easypj-sa -n easypj-prod</code></td></tr>
                            <tr><td>⚡</td><td><code>kubectl get sa -n &lt;ns&gt;</code></td><td>List all ServiceAccounts in a namespace</td><td><code>kubectl get sa -n easypj-prod</code></td></tr>
                            <tr><td></td><td><code>kubectl describe sa &lt;name&gt; -n &lt;ns&gt;</code></td><td>Show SA details including mounted secrets</td><td><code>kubectl describe sa easypj-sa -n easypj-prod</code></td></tr>
                            <tr><td>⚡</td><td><code>kubectl patch sa default -n &lt;ns&gt; -p '{"automountServiceAccountToken":false}'</code></td><td>Disable automatic token mount for default SA</td><td><code>kubectl patch sa default -n easypj-prod -p '{"automountServiceAccountToken":false}'</code></td></tr>
                            <tr><td></td><td><code>kubectl get sa &lt;name&gt; -n &lt;ns&gt; -o yaml | grep automount</code></td><td>Check if automount is enabled for a SA</td><td><code>kubectl get sa easypj-sa -n easypj-prod -o yaml | grep automount</code></td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>

                <h4>Role and RoleBinding Creation</h4>
                <div class="comparison-table">
                    <table>
                        <thead><tr><th style="width:8%;">⚡</th><th style="width:35%;">Command</th><th style="width:30%;">What It Does</th><th style="width:27%;">Example</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td>⚡</td><td><code>kubectl create role &lt;name&gt; --verb=&lt;verbs&gt; --resource=&lt;resources&gt; -n &lt;ns&gt;</code></td><td>Create a namespaced Role</td><td><code>kubectl create role pod-reader --verb=get,list,watch --resource=pods -n easypj-prod</code></td></tr>
                            <tr><td>⚡</td><td><code>kubectl create rolebinding &lt;name&gt; --role=&lt;role&gt; --serviceaccount=&lt;ns&gt;:&lt;sa&gt; -n &lt;ns&gt;</code></td><td>Bind a Role to a ServiceAccount</td><td><code>kubectl create rolebinding rb-pod-reader --role=pod-reader --serviceaccount=easypj-prod:easypj-sa -n easypj-prod</code></td></tr>
                            <tr><td>⚡</td><td><code>kubectl create clusterrole &lt;name&gt; --verb=&lt;verbs&gt; --resource=&lt;resources&gt;</code></td><td>Create a cluster-wide Role</td><td><code>kubectl create clusterrole node-reader --verb=get,list --resource=nodes</code></td></tr>
                            <tr><td>⚡</td><td><code>kubectl create clusterrolebinding &lt;name&gt; --clusterrole=&lt;role&gt; --serviceaccount=&lt;ns&gt;:&lt;sa&gt;</code></td><td>Bind a ClusterRole to a SA</td><td><code>kubectl create clusterrolebinding crb-node-reader --clusterrole=node-reader --serviceaccount=easypj-prod:easypj-sa</code></td></tr>
                            <tr><td></td><td><code>kubectl create role &lt;name&gt; --verb=&lt;verbs&gt; --resource=&lt;resources&gt; --resource-name=&lt;name&gt; -n &lt;ns&gt;</code></td><td>Create a Role scoped to a specific resource name</td><td><code>kubectl create role secret-reader --verb=get --resource=secrets --resource-name=easypj-db -n easypj-prod</code></td></tr>
