            <section class="section-block" id="sa-7">
                <h3 class="section-h">A.7 etcd Security Commands</h3>
                <p>Commands for interacting with etcd directly — encryption verification, backup, and certificate inspection. <strong>These require etcdctl and TLS certificates.</strong></p>

                <div class="comparison-table">
                    <table>
                        <thead><tr><th style="width:8%;">⚡</th><th style="width:35%;">Command</th><th style="width:30%;">What It Does</th><th style="width:27%;">Example</th></tr></thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td>⚡</td><td><code>ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl --endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379 --cacert=&lt;ca&gt; --cert=&lt;cert&gt; --key=&lt;key&gt; get /registry/secrets/&lt;ns&gt;/&lt;name&gt;</code></td><td>Read a Secret directly from etcd</td><td><code>ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl --endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379 --cacert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/ca.crt --cert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.crt --key=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.key get /registry/secrets/easypj-prod/easypj-secrets</code></td></tr>
                            <tr><td>⚡</td><td><code>ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl ... get &lt;key&gt; | hexdump -C</code></td><td>Hex dump etcd value to verify encryption</td><td>Pipe <code>etcdctl get</code> output to <code>hexdump -C</code>. Encrypted data shows garbled binary with <code>k8s:enc:</code> prefix.</td></tr>
                            <tr><td></td><td><code>ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl ... get /registry/secrets/ --prefix --keys-only</code></td><td>List all Secrets stored in etcd</td><td>Shows all secret keys — but encrypted values require the API server to decrypt</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>⚡</td><td><code>ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl ... snapshot save &lt;file&gt;</code></td><td>Create an etcd backup snapshot</td><td><code>ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl --endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379 --cacert=ca.crt --cert=server.crt --key=server.key snapshot save /backup/etcd-$(date +%Y%m%d).db</code></td></tr>
                            <tr><td></td><td><code>ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl ... snapshot status &lt;file&gt;</code></td><td>Check snapshot integrity and metadata</td><td><code>ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl snapshot status /backup/etcd-backup.db</code></td></tr>
                            <tr><td></td><td><code>ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl ... snapshot restore &lt;file&gt; --data-dir=&lt;dir&gt;</code></td><td>Restore etcd from a snapshot</td><td><code>ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl snapshot restore /backup/etcd-backup.db --data-dir=/var/lib/etcd-restored</code></td></tr>
                            <tr><td></td><td><code>ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl ... endpoint health</code></td><td>Check etcd cluster health</td><td><code>ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl --endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379 --cacert=ca.crt --cert=server.crt --key=server.key endpoint health</code></td></tr>
                            <tr><td></td><td><code>ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl ... endpoint status --write-out=table</code></td><td>Show etcd cluster status (leader, size, version)</td><td><code>ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl --endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379 --cacert=ca.crt --cert=server.crt --key=server.key endpoint status --write-out=table</code></td></tr>
                            <tr><td></td><td><code>ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl ... member list</code></td><td>List all etcd cluster members</td><td><code>ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl --endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379 --cacert=ca.crt --cert=server.crt --key=server.key member list</code></td></tr>
                            <tr><td></td><td><code>openssl x509 -in /etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.crt -text -noout | grep -A2 Validity</code></td><td>Check etcd certificate expiration</td><td><code>openssl x509 -in /etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.crt -text -noout | grep -A2 Validity</code></td></tr>
                            <tr><td></td><td><code>openssl x509 -in /etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/peer.crt -text -noout | grep DNS</code></td><td>Check etcd peer certificate SANs</td><td><code>openssl x509 -in /etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/peer.crt -text -noout | grep DNS</code></td></tr>
                            <tr><td></td><td><code>ls -la /etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/</code></td><td>List etcd certificates and keys</td><td><code>ls -la /etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/</code></td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>

                <div class="info-box warning">
                    <h5>⚠️ etcd Access Requires Certificates</h5>
                    <p>Every <code>etcdctl</code> command requires three certificate flags: <code>--cacert</code>, <code>--cert</code>, and <code>--key</code>. These are almost always at <code>/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/</code>. If you forget even one, etcdctl returns <code>context deadline exceeded</code> or <code>connection refused</code> — this means your TLS is misconfigured, not that etcd is down. Create an alias: <code>alias etcdctl-secure='ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl --endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379 --cacert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/ca.crt --cert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.crt --key=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.key'</code> to save typing on the exam.</p>
                </div>
            </section>
