            <!-- ═══════════ SECTION E.1 ═══════════ -->
            <section class="section-block" id="se-1">
                <h3 class="section-h">E.1 Namespace with PSS Labels</h3>
                <p>Creates the <strong>easypj-prod</strong> namespace with Pod Security Standards Restricted enforcement. All three modes applied: enforce (block), warn (notify), audit (log).</p>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-lang">YAML — namespace-easypj-prod.yaml</span></div>
                    <pre><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: easypj-prod
  labels:
    pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce: restricted
    pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce-version: v1.30
    pod-security.kubernetes.io/warn: restricted
    pod-security.kubernetes.io/warn-version: v1.30
    pod-security.kubernetes.io/audit: restricted
    pod-security.kubernetes.io/audit-version: v1.30</code></pre>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- ═══════════ SECTION E.2 ═══════════ -->
            <section class="section-block" id="se-2">
                <h3 class="section-h">E.2 RBAC: ServiceAccounts, Roles, RoleBindings</h3>
                <p>Dedicated ServiceAccounts for easypj, PostgreSQL, and CI/CD with least-privilege RBAC. <strong>Note:</strong> application SAs have automount disabled — no API access from app pods.</p>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-lang">YAML — rbac-easypj.yaml</span></div>
                    <pre><code class="language-yaml">---
apiVersion: v1
kind: ServiceAccount
metadata:
  name: easypj-sa
  namespace: easypj-prod
automountServiceAccountToken: false
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: ServiceAccount
metadata:
  name: postgres-sa
  namespace: easypj-prod
automountServiceAccountToken: false
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: ServiceAccount
metadata:
  name: cicd-deployer
  namespace: easypj-prod
---
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: Role
metadata:
  name: cicd-updater
  namespace: easypj-prod
rules:
- apiGroups: ["apps"]
  resources: ["deployments"]
  verbs: ["get", "list", "watch", "update", "patch"]
  resourceNames: ["easypj", "postgres"]
---
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: RoleBinding
metadata:
  name: cicd-updater-binding
  namespace: easypj-prod
subjects:
- kind: ServiceAccount
  name: cicd-deployer
  namespace: easypj-prod
roleRef:
  kind: Role
  name: cicd-updater
  apiGroup: rbac.authorization.k8s.io</code></pre>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- ═══════════ SECTION E.3 ═══════════ -->
            <section class="section-block" id="se-3">
                <h3 class="section-h">E.3 NetworkPolicies: Default Deny + Specific Allow Rules</h3>
                <p>Full microsegmentation for the easypj namespace. Default-deny-all as foundation, then explicit allow rules for ingress, database, cache, DNS, and monitoring.</p>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-lang">YAML — networkpolicies-easypj.yaml</span></div>
                    <pre><code class="language-yaml">---
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: default-deny-all
  namespace: easypj-prod
spec:
  podSelector: {}
  policyTypes: [Ingress, Egress]
---
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: allow-dns
  namespace: easypj-prod
spec:
  podSelector: {}
  policyTypes: [Egress]
  egress:
  - to:
    - namespaceSelector:
        matchLabels:
          kubernetes.io/metadata.name: kube-system
      podSelector:
        matchLabels:
          k8s-app: kube-dns
    ports:
    - protocol: UDP
      port: 53
---
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: allow-ingress-to-easypj
  namespace: easypj-prod
spec:
  podSelector:
    matchLabels:
      app: easypj
  policyTypes: [Ingress]
  ingress:
  - from:
    - namespaceSelector:
        matchLabels:
          name: ingress-nginx
    ports:
    - protocol: TCP
      port: 8000
---
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: allow-easypj-to-postgres
  namespace: easypj-prod
spec:
  podSelector:
    matchLabels:
      app: easypj
  policyTypes: [Egress]
  egress:
  - to:
    - podSelector:
        matchLabels:
          app: postgres
    ports:
    - protocol: TCP
      port: 5432
---
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: allow-easypj-to-redis
  namespace: easypj-prod
spec:
  podSelector:
    matchLabels:
      app: easypj
  policyTypes: [Egress]
  egress:
  - to:
    - podSelector:
        matchLabels:
          app: redis
    ports:
    - protocol: TCP
      port: 6379</code></pre>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- ═══════════ SECTION E.4 ═══════════ -->
            <section class="section-block" id="se-4">
                <h3 class="section-h">E.4 Secrets (Encrypted at Rest Reference)</h3>
                <p>Kubernetes Secrets for sensitive easypj configuration. These are encrypted at rest via EncryptionConfiguration (E.13). <strong>Never commit actual secret values to Git.</strong></p>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-lang">YAML — secrets-easypj.yaml</span></div>
                    <pre><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: easypj-secrets
  namespace: easypj-prod
type: Opaque
stringData:
  django-secret-key: "&lt;generate-with-openssl-rand-base64-48&gt;"
  db-password: "&lt;generate-secure-password&gt;"
  redis-password: "&lt;generate-secure-password&gt;"
  email-host-password: "&lt;smtp-password&gt;"
# ⚠️ After creating, delete this file from local machine
# ⚠️ Verify encryption: etcdctl get /registry/secrets/easypj-prod/easypj-secrets | hexdump -C</code></pre>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- ═══════════ SECTION E.5 ═══════════ -->
            <section class="section-block" id="se-5">
                <h3 class="section-h">E.5 ConfigMap (Non-Sensitive Django Settings)</h3>
                <p>Non-sensitive application configuration. Database host, Redis host, allowed hosts, and Django settings that are safe to store in plaintext.</p>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-lang">YAML — configmap-easypj.yaml</span></div>
                    <pre><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: easypj-config
  namespace: easypj-prod
data:
  DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE: "easypj.settings"
  DJANGO_ALLOWED_HOSTS: "jobs.easypj.com,localhost,127.0.0.1"
  DJANGO_DEBUG: "False"
  DB_HOST: "postgres.easypj-prod.svc.cluster.local"
  DB_PORT: "5432"
  DB_NAME: "easypj"
  REDIS_HOST: "redis.easypj-prod.svc.cluster.local"
  REDIS_PORT: "6379"
  EMAIL_HOST: "smtp.easypj.com"
  EMAIL_PORT: "587"
  EMAIL_USE_TLS: "True"
  STATIC_ROOT: "/app/staticfiles"
  MEDIA_ROOT: "/app/media"</code></pre>
