            <!-- ═══════════ SECTION E.6 ═══════════ -->
            <section class="section-block" id="se-6">
                <h3 class="section-h">E.6 Hardened Django Deployment (Full Security Context)</h3>
                <p>The main easypj Django application deployment with <strong>complete CKS Restricted security context</strong>: non-root user, read-only filesystem, dropped capabilities, Seccomp RuntimeDefault, and dedicated ServiceAccount.</p>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-lang">YAML — deployment-easypj.yaml</span></div>
                    <pre><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: easypj
  namespace: easypj-prod
  labels:
    app: easypj
spec:
  replicas: 3
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: easypj
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: easypj
    spec:
      serviceAccountName: easypj-sa
      automountServiceAccountToken: false
      securityContext:
        runAsNonRoot: true
        runAsUser: 1000
        runAsGroup: 1000
        fsGroup: 1000
        seccompProfile:
          type: RuntimeDefault
      containers:
      - name: easypj
        image: &lt;registry&gt;/easypj@sha256:&lt;digest&gt;
        ports:
        - containerPort: 8000
          protocol: TCP
        securityContext:
          runAsNonRoot: true
          runAsUser: 1000
          allowPrivilegeEscalation: false
          readOnlyRootFilesystem: true
          capabilities:
            drop: ["ALL"]
        envFrom:
        - configMapRef:
            name: easypj-config
        env:
        - name: SECRET_KEY
          valueFrom:
            secretKeyRef:
              name: easypj-secrets
              key: django-secret-key
        - name: DB_PASSWORD
          valueFrom:
            secretKeyRef:
              name: easypj-secrets
              key: db-password
        - name: REDIS_PASSWORD
          valueFrom:
            secretKeyRef:
              name: easypj-secrets
              key: redis-password
        resources:
          requests:
            memory: "256Mi"
            cpu: "250m"
          limits:
            memory: "512Mi"
            cpu: "500m"
        livenessProbe:
          httpGet:
            path: /healthz/
            port: 8000
          initialDelaySeconds: 30
          periodSeconds: 10
        readinessProbe:
          httpGet:
            path: /readiness/
            port: 8000
          initialDelaySeconds: 10
          periodSeconds: 5
        volumeMounts:
        - name: tmp
          mountPath: /tmp
        - name: runtime
          mountPath: /var/run
        - name: media
          mountPath: /app/media
      volumes:
      - name: tmp
        emptyDir: {}
      - name: runtime
        emptyDir: {}
      - name: media
        persistentVolumeClaim:
          claimName: easypj-media-pvc</code></pre>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- ═══════════ SECTION E.7 ═══════════ -->
            <section class="section-block" id="se-7">
                <h3 class="section-h">E.7 Django Service (ClusterIP Only)</h3>
                <p>Internal ClusterIP service for the Django application. <strong>Not exposed externally</strong> — the Ingress controller (E.9) handles external traffic with TLS termination.</p>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-lang">YAML — service-easypj.yaml</span></div>
                    <pre><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: easypj
  namespace: easypj-prod
  labels:
    app: easypj
spec:
  type: ClusterIP
  selector:
    app: easypj
  ports:
  - name: http
    protocol: TCP
    port: 8000
    targetPort: 8000</code></pre>
