                <h4>⚡ Exam Day Mental Warmup — 10 Commands to Type Before You Start</h4>
                <p>During the check-in waiting period (proctor is verifying other candidates), you can't use the terminal but you CAN mentally rehearse. Recite these 10 commands:</p>
                <div class="code-block-wrapper">
                    <div class="code-block-header"><span class="code-lang">Bash — Mental warmup: recite these in order before the exam starts</span></div>
                    <pre><code class="language-bash"># 1. Context switch (THE RITUAL — do this for EVERY task)
kubectl config use-context &lt;name&gt;
kubectl config current-context

# 2. Quick pod with security context
kubectl run test --image=nginx --restart=Never --dry-run=client -o yaml | vi -

# 3. RBAC creation (NEVER write YAML from scratch)
kubectl create role r1 --verb=get,list --resource=pods -n ns --dry-run=client -o yaml

# 4. RBAC verification
kubectl auth can-i get pods -n ns --as=system:serviceaccount:ns:sa

# 5. NetworkPolicy test
kubectl run test --rm -it --image=busybox --restart=Never -- wget -qO- --timeout=5 &lt;url&gt;

# 6. Falco rules — always edit LOCAL file
vi /etc/falco/falco_rules.local.yaml

# 7. Trivy scan
trivy image --severity CRITICAL,HIGH &lt;image&gt;

# 8. API server edit — add BOTH flag AND volume mount
vi /etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-apiserver.yaml

# 9. etcd verification
ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl --endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379 \
  --cacert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/ca.crt \
  --cert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.crt \
  --key=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.key \
  get /registry/secrets/ns/name | hexdump -C

# 10. Namespace PSS label
kubectl label ns &lt;name&gt; pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce=restricted</code></pre>
