            <!-- ============ DOMAIN 1: CLUSTER SETUP (10 Labs) ============ -->
            <section class="section-block" id="lab-d1">
                <h3 class="section-h">H.2 Domain 1 — Cluster Setup Labs (10 labs, CKS 10%)</h3>
                <p style="color:#8b949e;margin-bottom:16px;">Focus: NetworkPolicy, RBAC, TLS, Dashboard security, etcd backup/restore, cluster upgrades. These labs build the foundational muscle memory for 10% of the exam.</p>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 1.1</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 10 min — NetworkPolicy: Default-Deny + DNS + App Rules</strong><br>Create namespace <code>secure-lab</code>. Apply a default-deny-all NetworkPolicy. Then add rules allowing: (a) DNS from CoreDNS, (b) ingress to pods labeled <code>app: web</code> from pods labeled <code>app: gateway</code> on port 8080, (c) egress from <code>app: web</code> to <code>app: db</code> on port 5432. Verify connectivity works ONLY for allowed paths.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary>
                    <div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">kubectl create ns secure-lab
# Default-deny
kubectl apply -f - &lt;&lt;EOF
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata: {name: default-deny, namespace: secure-lab}
spec: {podSelector: {}, policyTypes: [Ingress, Egress]}
EOF
# DNS allow
kubectl apply -f - &lt;&lt;EOF
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata: {name: allow-dns, namespace: secure-lab}
spec:
  podSelector: {}
  policyTypes: [Egress]
  egress:
  - to: [{namespaceSelector: {matchLabels: {kubernetes.io/metadata.name: kube-system}}, podSelector: {k8s-app: kube-dns}}]
    ports: [{protocol: UDP, port: 53}]
EOF
# Run test pods and verify</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 1.2</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 8 min — RBAC: Least Privilege for CI/CD</strong><br>Create SA <code>cicd-bot</code> in <code>staging</code> namespace. Grant ONLY: get/list/watch/update/patch on Deployments, create/update Secrets. No other permissions. Verify with <code>kubectl auth can-i</code> that it CAN update deployments but CANNOT delete pods or list secrets.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">kubectl create ns staging
kubectl create sa cicd-bot -n staging
kubectl create role cicd-deployer -n staging --verb=get,list,watch,update,patch --resource=deployments
kubectl create rolebinding cicd-bind --role=cicd-deployer --serviceaccount=staging:cicd-bot -n staging
kubectl auth can-i update deployments --as=system:serviceaccount:staging:cicd-bot -n staging
kubectl auth can-i delete pods --as=system:serviceaccount:staging:cicd-bot -n staging  # MUST be "no"</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 1.3</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 12 min — etcd Backup & Restore</strong><br>Take an etcd snapshot. Create a Secret. Delete the Secret. Restore etcd from the snapshot. Verify the Secret is back. Time includes snapshot, restore, and verification.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl --cacert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/ca.crt --cert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.crt --key=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.key snapshot save /tmp/backup.db
kubectl create secret generic test-backup --from-literal=k=v
kubectl delete secret test-backup
mv /etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-apiserver.yaml /tmp/
ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl snapshot restore /tmp/backup.db --data-dir=/var/lib/etcd-restored
# Edit etcd.yaml to point --data-dir=/var/lib/etcd-restored
mv /tmp/kube-apiserver.yaml /etc/kubernetes/manifests/
kubectl get secret test-backup  # MUST exist</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 1.4</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 10 min — Cluster Upgrade Simulation</strong><br>Given cluster v1.29.x, upgrade the control plane to v1.30.x. Then upgrade kubelet on one worker. Verify all nodes show Ready with new version. Take etcd snapshot BEFORE upgrade.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl snapshot save /tmp/pre-upgrade.db
apt-mark unhold kubeadm && apt-get update && apt-get install -y kubeadm=1.30.x-00 && apt-mark hold kubeadm
kubeadm upgrade plan
kubeadm upgrade apply v1.30.x
kubectl drain worker01 --ignore-daemonsets --delete-emptydir-data
apt-get install -y kubelet=1.30.x-00 kubectl=1.30.x-00
systemctl restart kubelet && kubectl uncordon worker01
kubectl get nodes  # All Ready, all v1.30.x</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 1.5</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 6 min — TLS Secret + Ingress</strong><br>Generate a self-signed TLS cert for <code>lab.easypj.com</code>. Create TLS Secret <code>lab-tls</code>. Create an Ingress that uses this Secret for TLS termination. Curl the endpoint with <code>--resolve</code> to verify TLS works.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">openssl req -x509 -nodes -days 365 -newkey rsa:2048 -keyout lab.key -out lab.crt -subj "/CN=lab.easypj.com"
kubectl create secret tls lab-tls --cert=lab.crt --key=lab.key -n default
kubectl create ingress lab-tls --class=nginx --rule="lab.easypj.com/*=web-svc:80,tls=lab-tls"
curl -k --resolve lab.easypj.com:443:&lt;INGRESS-IP&gt; https://lab.easypj.com</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 1.6</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 8 min — ServiceAccount Zero-Privilege Setup</strong><br>Create SA <code>no-api</code> with <code>automountServiceAccountToken: false</code>. Create a pod using this SA. Verify: (a) <code>/var/run/secrets/kubernetes.io/serviceaccount/token</code> does NOT exist, (b) <code>kubectl auth can-i --as=system:serviceaccount:default:no-api get pods</code> returns "no".</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">kubectl create sa no-api
kubectl patch sa no-api -p '{"automountServiceAccountToken": false}'
kubectl run test --image=busybox --restart=Never --command -- sleep 300 --serviceaccount=no-api
kubectl exec test -- ls /var/run/secrets/kubernetes.io/serviceaccount/  # MUST fail
kubectl auth can-i get pods --as=system:serviceaccount:default:no-api  # MUST return "no"</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 1.7</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 10 min — Dashboard Security Audit</strong><br>Deploy Kubernetes Dashboard in namespace <code>kubernetes-dashboard</code>. Ensure: (a) <code>--enable-skip-login</code> is NOT set, (b) Dashboard SA has NO cluster-admin, (c) Dashboard Service is ClusterIP (not LoadBalancer), (d) NetworkPolicy restricts ingress to dashboard pod.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes/dashboard/v2.7.0/aio/deploy/recommended.yaml
kubectl get deploy kubernetes-dashboard -n kubernetes-dashboard -o yaml | grep skip-login
kubectl auth can-i --list -n kubernetes-dashboard --as=system:serviceaccount:kubernetes-dashboard:kubernetes-dashboard | grep -v "\[\]"
kubectl get svc kubernetes-dashboard -n kubernetes-dashboard  # Must be ClusterIP
kubectl apply -f dashboard-networkpolicy.yaml  # Restrict ingress</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 1.8</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 5 min — Anonymous Access Verification</strong><br>Verify anonymous access is disabled on the API server. Test with curl WITHOUT credentials. Then check the flag in the API server manifest.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">curl -k https://localhost:6443/api  # Must return 401 Unauthorized
grep anonymous-auth /etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-apiserver.yaml  # Must show --anonymous-auth=false</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 1.9</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 7 min — ClusterRole vs Role: Cross-Namespace Access</strong><br>Create ClusterRole <code>pod-reader</code> (get/list pods). Create RoleBinding in <code>ns1</code> to SA <code>reader</code> in <code>ns2</code>. Verify SA can read pods in ns1 but NOT in ns2.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">kubectl create clusterrole pod-reader --verb=get,list --resource=pods
kubectl create ns ns1 && kubectl create ns ns2
kubectl create sa reader -n ns2
kubectl create rolebinding pod-reader-ns1 --clusterrole=pod-reader --serviceaccount=ns2:reader -n ns1
kubectl auth can-i get pods --as=system:serviceaccount:ns2:reader -n ns1  # yes
kubectl auth can-i get pods --as=system:serviceaccount:ns2:reader -n ns2  # no</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 1.10</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 8 min — API Server Flag Audit</strong><br>SSH to control plane. List ALL security-relevant API server flags. Identify: authorization-mode, anonymous-auth, enable-admission-plugins. If any are missing or insecure (e.g., AlwaysAllow), fix them. Verify the API server restarts successfully.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">cat /etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-apiserver.yaml | grep -E "authorization-mode|anonymous-auth|enable-admission-plugins"
# Expected: --authorization-mode=Node,RBAC --anonymous-auth=false --enable-admission-plugins=NodeRestriction,...
kubectl get nodes  # Verify API server is healthy after changes</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- ============ DOMAIN 2: CLUSTER HARDENING (10 Labs) ============ -->
            <section class="section-block" id="lab-d2">
                <h3 class="section-h">H.3 Domain 2 — Cluster Hardening Labs (10 labs, CKS 15%)</h3>
                <p style="color:#8b949e;margin-bottom:16px;">Focus: CIS benchmarks, kube-bench, RBAC, admission controllers, PSP/PSS migration, NodeRestriction, audit logging. These are the most common exam tasks.</p>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 2.1</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 12 min — Run kube-bench & Fix All FAILs</strong><br>Run kube-bench as a Job against the master node. Identify every [FAIL]. Fix at least 5 FAILs: anonymous-auth, authorization-mode, audit-log-path, profiling, and one more. Re-run kube-bench to verify all former FAILs are now PASS.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aquasecurity/kube-bench/main/job.yaml
kubectl logs job/kube-bench | grep FAIL
# Fix each FAIL in /etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-apiserver.yaml
# Wait for restart, re-run kube-bench
kubectl delete job kube-bench && kubectl apply -f ...job.yaml
kubectl logs job/kube-bench | grep FAIL  # Should be empty or only informational</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 2.2</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 8 min — Kubelet Hardening</strong><br>Edit <code>/var/lib/kubelet/config.yaml</code>: disable anonymous-auth, set authorization-mode to Webhook, disable readOnlyPort (set to 0), enable protectKernelDefaults. Restart kubelet and verify with kube-bench node checks.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">vi /var/lib/kubelet/config.yaml
# Set: authentication.anonymous.enabled: false, authorization.mode: Webhook, readOnlyPort: 0, protectKernelDefaults: true
systemctl restart kubelet
kube-bench run --targets node --check 4.2.1,4.2.2,4.2.3,4.2.6</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 2.3</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 10 min — Enable NodeRestriction Admission Plugin</strong><br>Verify NodeRestriction is in the admission plugins list. If not, add it. Test: kubelet on worker01 should NOT be able to modify worker02's labels. Verify with <code>kubectl auth can-i</code>.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">grep enable-admission-plugins /etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-apiserver.yaml
# Add NodeRestriction if missing. Wait for restart.
kubectl auth can-i update nodes/worker02 --as=system:node:worker01  # MUST be "no"</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 2.4</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 10 min — Audit Policy: Secrets + RBAC Logging</strong><br>Create an audit policy that logs: (a) all Secret operations at Metadata level, (b) all RBAC changes at RequestResponse level, (c) nothing else. Configure API server to use it. Create a test Secret and verify it appears in audit logs.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: audit.k8s.io/v1
kind: Policy
rules:
- level: Metadata
  resources: [{group: "", resources: ["secrets"]}]
- level: RequestResponse
  resources: [{group: "rbac.authorization.k8s.io", resources: ["*"]}]
- level: None</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 2.5</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 6 min — SSH Hardening</strong><br>On each node: disable root SSH login, disable password authentication, disable X11 forwarding. Restart SSH. Verify root can't SSH with password.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">sed -i 's/^PermitRootLogin.*/PermitRootLogin no/' /etc/ssh/sshd_config
sed -i 's/^PasswordAuthentication.*/PasswordAuthentication no/' /etc/ssh/sshd_config
sed -i 's/^X11Forwarding.*/X11Forwarding no/' /etc/ssh/sshd_config
systemctl restart sshd</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 2.6</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 15 min — EncryptionConfiguration: Full Setup</strong><br>Create EncryptionConfiguration for Secrets using aescbc. Update API server manifest with flag, volumeMount, AND volume. Restart. Verify by reading etcd directly — data must be encrypted with k8s:enc:aescbc prefix.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">cat > /etc/kubernetes/encryption-config.yaml &lt;&lt;EOF
apiVersion: apiserver.config.k8s.io/v1
kind: EncryptionConfiguration
resources: [{resources: ["secrets"], providers: [{aescbc: {keys: [{name: key1, secret: $(head -c32 /dev/urandom | base64)}]}}, {identity: {}}]}]
EOF
# Edit kube-apiserver.yaml: add flag + volumeMount + volume
kubectl create secret generic test-enc --from-literal=k=v
ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl get /registry/secrets/default/test-enc | hexdump -C | head  # Must show k8s:enc:aescbc</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 2.7</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 8 min — RBAC Impersonation Audit</strong><br>Create a user with <code>impersonate</code> permission. Impersonate another user. Check audit logs for the impersonation event — verify the original username is preserved.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">kubectl create clusterrole impersonator --verb=impersonate --resource=users
kubectl create clusterrolebinding imp-bind --clusterrole=impersonator --user=auditor
kubectl get pods --as=system:admin  # Impersonate
cat /var/log/kubernetes/audit.log | jq 'select(.user.extra."authentication.k8s.io/original-username" != null)'</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 2.8</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 6 min — API Server Profiling Disable</strong><br>Verify <code>--profiling=false</code> on API server, controller-manager, and scheduler. If enabled, disable it. Verify /debug/pprof/ returns 404 or 403.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">grep profiling /etc/kubernetes/manifests/*.yaml
kubectl get --raw /debug/pprof/  # Must return 404 or empty</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 2.9</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 7 min — Static Pod Manifest Permission Fix</strong><br>Verify permissions on /etc/kubernetes/manifests/*.yaml are 600 and owned by root:root. Fix any that aren't.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">stat -c "%a %U:%G %n" /etc/kubernetes/manifests/*.yaml
chmod 600 /etc/kubernetes/manifests/*.yaml
chown root:root /etc/kubernetes/manifests/*.yaml</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 2.10</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 10 min — Audit Log Webhook Configuration</strong><br>Configure audit log webhook to ship events to a mock endpoint. Create webhook kubeconfig. Verify API server has --audit-webhook-config-file flag. Check API server logs for successful webhook connection.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">cat > /etc/kubernetes/audit-webhook.yaml &lt;&lt;EOF
apiVersion: v1; kind: Config; clusters: [{name: siem, cluster: {server: https://siem.easypj.com:8088}}]
users: [{name: webhook, user: {token: test-token}}]
contexts: [{context: {cluster: siem, user: webhook}, name: audit}]
current-context: audit
EOF
# Add --audit-webhook-config-file=/etc/kubernetes/audit-webhook.yaml to API server</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- ============ DOMAIN 3: SYSTEM HARDENING (8 Labs) ============ -->
            <section class="section-block" id="lab-d3">
                <h3 class="section-h">H.4 Domain 3 — System Hardening Labs (8 labs, CKS 15%)</h3>
                <p style="color:#8b949e;margin-bottom:16px;">Focus: AppArmor, Seccomp, kernel hardening, OS minimization. These labs require SSH access to nodes.</p>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 3.1</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 12 min — AppArmor: Write, Load, Apply, Test</strong><br>Write an AppArmor profile that allows read of /app/**, write to /tmp/**, and denies access to /etc/kubernetes/. Load it with apparmor_parser. Apply to a pod. Test that the pod CAN read /app but CANNOT read /etc/kubernetes.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">cat > /etc/apparmor.d/k8s-app &lt;&lt;EOF
profile k8s-app flags=(attach_disconnected) { #include &lt;abstractions/base&gt;  /app/** r,  /tmp/** rw,  deny /etc/kubernetes/** rw, }
EOF
apparmor_parser -q /etc/apparmor.d/k8s-app
kubectl run test --image=busybox --restart=Never --command -- sleep 300 --annotations="container.apparmor.security.beta.kubernetes.io/test: localhost/k8s-app"
kubectl exec test -- cat /etc/kubernetes/pki/ca.crt  # MUST fail "Permission denied"</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 3.2</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 10 min — Custom Seccomp Profile: Block mount + unshare</strong><br>Write a Seccomp profile blocking mount, umount2, unshare, and reboot. Save to /var/lib/kubelet/seccomp/. Apply to pod. Verify pod starts and unshare is blocked.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">cat > /var/lib/kubelet/seccomp/block-escape.json &lt;&lt;EOF
{"defaultAction":"SCMP_ACT_ALLOW","architectures":["SCMP_ARCH_X86_64"],"syscalls":[{"names":["mount","umount2","unshare","reboot","kexec_load"],"action":"SCMP_ACT_ERRNO"}]}
EOF
kubectl run secured --image=busybox --dry-run=client -o yaml | sed 's/containers:/securityContext:\n        seccompProfile: {type: Localhost, localhostProfile: block-escape.json}\n      containers:/' | kubectl apply -f -</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 3.3</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 8 min — Kernel Module Blacklisting</strong><br>Blacklist: cramfs, freevxfs, jffs2, hfs, hfsplus, squashfs, udf. Verify with <code>lsmod</code> they're not loaded. Set modules_disabled after verification.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">for mod in cramfs freevxfs jffs2 hfs hfsplus squashfs udf; do echo "blacklist $mod" >> /etc/modprobe.d/blacklist.conf; modprobe -r $mod 2>/dev/null; done
lsmod | grep -E "cramfs|freevxfs|jffs2|hfs|squashfs|udf"  # Should be empty
echo 1 > /proc/sys/kernel/modules_disabled  # Lock it</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 3.4</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 6 min — Port Minimization</strong><br>SSH to worker node. List all listening ports. Identify non-Kubernetes services. Stop and disable: FTP, SMTP, NFS, CUPS, avahi. Verify only kubelet, containerd, and SSH remain.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">ss -tulnp
systemctl stop vsftpd postfix nfs-server cups avahi-daemon 2>/dev/null
systemctl disable vsftpd postfix nfs-server cups avahi-daemon 2>/dev/null
ss -tulnp | grep -v -E "kubelet|containerd|sshd"  # Should be empty or minimal</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 3.5</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 8 min — AIDE: Initialize, Check, Update</strong><br>Install AIDE. Initialize the database. Modify /etc/hosts (simulate tampering). Run aide --check and verify the modification is detected. Update the database after the "legitimate" change.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">apt-get install -y aide
aide --init && cp /var/lib/aide/aide.db.new.gz /var/lib/aide/aide.db.gz
echo "10.0.0.50 bad.host.com" >> /etc/hosts  # Simulate tampering
aide --check  # Reports /etc/hosts changed
aide --update && cp /var/lib/aide/aide.db.new.gz /var/lib/aide/aide.db.gz  # Accept change</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 3.6</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 5 min — Kernel Hardening: sysctl Security Settings</strong><br>Set: kernel.randomize_va_space=2, kernel.kptr_restrict=2, kernel.dmesg_restrict=1, net.ipv4.tcp_syncookies=1. Persist in /etc/sysctl.d/99-security.conf.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">cat > /etc/sysctl.d/99-security.conf &lt;&lt;EOF
kernel.randomize_va_space=2
kernel.kptr_restrict=2
kernel.dmesg_restrict=1
net.ipv4.tcp_syncookies=1
net.ipv4.ip_forward=0
EOF
sysctl --system</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 3.7</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 6 min — Remove Unnecessary Packages</strong><br>List all installed packages. Remove unnecessary ones: ftp, telnet, nfs-common, rpcbind, bluetooth, wireless-tools. Verify removed packages are gone.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">apt list --installed | grep -E "ftp|telnet|nfs|rpcbind|bluetooth|wireless"
apt remove --purge ftp telnet nfs-common rpcbind bluetooth wireless-tools -y</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 3.8</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 10 min — Seccomp RuntimeDefault + Profile Debugging</strong><br>Deploy a pod with RuntimeDefault Seccomp. If it crashes, debug which syscall is blocked (dmesg), create a custom profile allowing that syscall, and redeploy. Verify the pod runs.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">kubectl run test --image=nginx --dry-run=client -o yaml | sed 's/containers:/securityContext:\n        seccompProfile: {type: RuntimeDefault}\n      containers:/' | kubectl apply -f -
kubectl logs test  # Check for errors
dmesg | grep -i seccomp  # Find blocked syscall
# Create custom profile allowing the blocked syscall, redeploy</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- ============ DOMAIN 4: MICROSERVICE VULNERABILITIES (10 Labs) ============ -->
            <section class="section-block" id="lab-d4">
                <h3 class="section-h">H.5 Domain 4 — Minimize Microservice Vulnerabilities Labs (10 labs, CKS 20%)</h3>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 4.1</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 8 min — PSS Restricted: Label + Fix Violations</strong><br>Label namespace <code>prod-lab</code> with enforce=restricted. Deploy a pod running as root — it must be REJECTED. Fix the pod spec to satisfy Restricted (non-root, Seccomp, drop ALL caps, readOnlyRoot). Redeploy — must succeed.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">kubectl create ns prod-lab
kubectl label ns prod-lab pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce=restricted
kubectl label ns prod-lab pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce-version=v1.30
# Deploy root pod — REJECTED
kubectl run root-pod --image=nginx -n prod-lab  # FAILS
# Fix and redeploy with securityContext (runAsNonRoot, seccomp, drop ALL, readOnly)
</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 4.2</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 7 min — Full SecurityContext Implementation</strong><br>Deploy a pod with the CKS golden securityContext: runAsNonRoot:true, runAsUser:1000, allowPrivilegeEscalation:false, readOnlyRootFilesystem:true, capabilities.drop:[ALL], seccompProfile.type:RuntimeDefault. Add emptyDir for /tmp. Verify: can write to /tmp, cannot write to /etc.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-yaml">securityContext:
  runAsNonRoot: true; runAsUser: 1000; allowPrivilegeEscalation: false
  readOnlyRootFilesystem: true; capabilities: {drop: [ALL]}
  seccompProfile: {type: RuntimeDefault}
volumeMounts: [{name: tmp, mountPath: /tmp}]
volumes: [{name: tmp, emptyDir: {}}]</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 4.3</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 8 min — Secrets Encryption Verification</strong><br>Create a Secret. Read it via kubectl (should show base64). Read it via etcdctl directly — must show encrypted data with k8s:enc prefix. If not encrypted, enable EncryptionConfiguration and retest.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">kubectl create secret generic verify-enc --from-literal=password=SuperSecret123
kubectl get secret verify-enc -o jsonpath='{.data.password}' | base64 -d  # Shows plaintext
ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl get /registry/secrets/default/verify-enc | hexdump -C | head  # Must show k8s:enc</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 4.4</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 10 min — gVisor RuntimeClass: Setup + Apply</strong><br>Install gVisor (or verify it's installed). Create RuntimeClass <code>gvisor</code> with handler <code>runsc</code>. Deploy a pod using this RuntimeClass. Verify with <code>dmesg | grep gvisor</code> or check /proc/1/cgroup inside the pod.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">kubectl apply -f - &lt;&lt;EOF
apiVersion: node.k8s.io/v1; kind: RuntimeClass; metadata: {name: gvisor}; handler: runsc
EOF
kubectl run sandboxed --image=nginx --overrides='{"spec":{"runtimeClassName":"gvisor"}}'
kubectl exec sandboxed -- dmesg | grep -i gvisor</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 4.5</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 8 min — Istio mTLS: STRICT Mode</strong><br>Install Istio (or use existing). Label namespace <code>mtls-test</code> for injection. Deploy two pods. Apply PeerAuthentication STRICT. Verify mTLS is active with <code>istioctl authn tls-check</code>.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">kubectl create ns mtls-test
kubectl label ns mtls-test istio-injection=enabled
kubectl apply -f - &lt;&lt;EOF
apiVersion: security.istio.io/v1beta1
kind: PeerAuthentication; metadata: {name: strict, namespace: mtls-test}
spec: {mtls: {mode: STRICT}}
EOF
kubectl run a --image=nginx -n mtls-test; kubectl run b --image=nginx -n mtls-test
istioctl authn tls-check a -n mtls-test</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 4.6</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 6 min — Image Digest Pinning</strong><br>Deploy a pod using image tag <code>nginx:latest</code>. Find its digest with <code>kubectl get pod -o json</code>. Update the deployment to use the digest instead of the tag. Verify the pod uses the digest.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">kubectl create deploy nginx --image=nginx:latest
DIGEST=$(kubectl get pod -l app=nginx -o jsonpath='{.items[0].status.containerStatuses[0].imageID}' | cut -d'@' -f2)
kubectl set image deploy/nginx nginx=nginx@$DIGEST
kubectl get deploy nginx -o jsonpath='{.spec.template.spec.containers[0].image}'  # Must show @sha256</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 4.7</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 8 min — Kyverno: Disallow Privileged Pods</strong><br>Install Kyverno. Create a ClusterPolicy that rejects any pod with <code>privileged: true</code>. Test: deploy a privileged pod — must be REJECTED. Deploy a non-privileged pod — must succeed.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">kubectl apply -f https://github.com/kyverno/kyverno/releases/latest/download/install.yaml
kubectl apply -f - &lt;&lt;EOF
apiVersion: kyverno.io/v1; kind: ClusterPolicy; metadata: {name: disallow-privileged}
spec:
  validationFailureAction: Enforce
  rules:
  - name: no-privileged; match: {any: [{resources: {kinds: [Pod]}}]}
    validate: {message: "Privileged pods are not allowed", pattern: {spec: {containers: [{securityContext: {privileged: false}}]}}}
EOF</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 4.8</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 6 min — NetworkPolicy Egress Lockdown</strong><br>Create NetworkPolicy that allows pods labeled <code>app: web</code> to ONLY communicate with: DNS (UDP 53), pods labeled <code>app: db</code> on port 5432. Block everything else. Verify: web pod CANNOT curl google.com.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1; kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata: {name: egress-lockdown, namespace: default}
spec:
  podSelector: {app: web}; policyTypes: [Egress]
  egress:
  - to: [{namespaceSelector: {matchLabels: {name: kube-system}}, podSelector: {k8s-app: kube-dns}}]; ports: [{protocol: UDP, port: 53}]
  - to: [{podSelector: {app: db}}]; ports: [{protocol: TCP, port: 5432}]</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 4.9</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 12 min — Vault Integration</strong><br>Install Vault in dev mode. Enable Kubernetes auth. Create a role. Deploy a pod with Vault sidecar that reads a secret from Vault and writes it to a shared volume. Verify the secret appears in the pod.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">helm install vault hashicorp/vault --set server.dev.enabled=true
kubectl exec vault-0 -- vault auth enable kubernetes
kubectl exec vault-0 -- vault write auth/kubernetes/config token_reviewer_jwt="$(cat /var/run/secrets/kubernetes.io/serviceaccount/token)" kubernetes_host=https://kubernetes.default.svc
kubectl exec vault-0 -- vault kv put secret/easypj/db password=secret123</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 4.10</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 6 min — ServiceAccount Token Projection</strong><br>Deploy a pod with a projected ServiceAccount token with expirationSeconds: 600. Verify the token exists. Wait 11 minutes and verify the token has been rotated (new token, different signature).</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-yaml">volumes:
- name: token; projected:
    sources: [{serviceAccountToken: {path: token, expirationSeconds: 600, audience: api}}]
containers:
- volumeMounts: [{name: token, mountPath: /var/run/secrets/tokens, readOnly: true}]</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- ============ DOMAIN 5: SUPPLY CHAIN (10 Labs) ============ -->
            <section class="section-block" id="lab-d5">
                <h3 class="section-h">H.6 Domain 5 — Supply Chain Security Labs (10 labs, CKS 20%)</h3>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 5.1</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 8 min — Trivy: Scan, Block, Fix</strong><br>Scan image <code>nginx:1.21</code> with Trivy. Note CRITICAL CVEs. Update to <code>nginx:1.25-alpine</code>. Rescan. Verify CRITICAL count dropped significantly. Write a CI pipeline step that blocks on CRITICAL with --exit-code 1.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">trivy image --severity CRITICAL nginx:1.21
trivy image --severity CRITICAL nginx:1.25-alpine
# CI step:
trivy image --severity CRITICAL --exit-code 1 $IMAGE  # Fails pipeline if CRITICAL found</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 5.2</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 10 min — Cosign: Keyless Sign + Verify</strong><br>Generate a test image. Sign it with cosign keyless (COSIGN_EXPERIMENTAL=1). Push to registry. Verify the signature. Then verify with specific OIDC identity. Attempt to verify with wrong identity — must FAIL.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">docker build -t ghcr.io/easypj/test:v1 .
docker push ghcr.io/easypj/test:v1
COSIGN_EXPERIMENTAL=1 cosign sign ghcr.io/easypj/test@sha256:...
cosign verify ghcr.io/easypj/test@sha256:...
cosign verify --certificate-identity=wrong@email.com ghcr.io/easypj/test@sha256:...  # MUST fail</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 5.3</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 6 min — SBOM: Generate + Attach</strong><br>Generate SBOM for an image with syft (spdx-json format). Attach SBOM to the image with cosign attach sbom. Download and verify the SBOM is retrievable.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">syft nginx:latest -o spdx-json > sbom.json
cosign attach sbom --sbom sbom.json nginx@sha256:...
cosign download sbom nginx@sha256:... | jq .  # Verify it's retrievable</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 5.4</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 8 min — kubesec: Score 3→8</strong><br>Scan a deliberately insecure pod YAML with kubesec (score ~2-3). Fix: add runAsNonRoot, readOnlyRootFilesystem, drop ALL caps, Seccomp, resource limits. Rescan. Target score: 8+.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">kubesec scan insecure-pod.yaml  # ~3/10
# Edit: add securityContext fields
kubesec scan hardened-pod.yaml  # ~8+/10</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 5.5</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 10 min — Gatekeeper: Approved Registries Only</strong><br>Create ConstraintTemplate + Constraint that only allows images from <code>registry.easypj.com</code>. Test: deploy nginx from Docker Hub — REJECTED. Deploy image from approved registry — ALLOWED.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-rego">package k8sallowedrepos
violation[{"msg": msg}] {
  container := input.review.object.spec.containers[_]
  not startswith(container.image, "registry.easypj.com/")
  msg := sprintf("disallowed registry: %v", [container.image])
}</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 5.6</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 8 min — conftest: Rego Policy in CI</strong><br>Write Rego policy that blocks pods without runAsNonRoot. Test with conftest on a pod YAML. Fail the test (pod without runAsNonRoot). Fix the YAML. Pass the test.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-rego">package main
deny[msg] {
  container := input.spec.containers[_]
  not container.securityContext.runAsNonRoot == true
  msg := sprintf("runAsNonRoot must be true for container %v", [container.name])
}</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 5.7</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 6 min — ImagePolicyWebhook Configuration</strong><br>Create ImagePolicyWebhook config file. Add admission plugin to API server. Verify the webhook is called on pod creation. Test with an allowed image and a denied image.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash"># Add to API server: --enable-admission-plugins=...,ImagePolicyWebhook
# --admission-control-config-file=/etc/kubernetes/image-policy.yaml
# Create config file with kubeconfig pointing to webhook backend</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 5.8</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 10 min — kube-linter: Audit Manifests</strong><br>Scan a directory of Kubernetes manifests with kube-linter. Identify: pods running as root, missing resource limits, privilege escalation allowed. Fix all HIGH severity findings. Rescan — zero HIGH findings.</div>
