            <!-- ============ DOMAIN 6: RUNTIME SECURITY (8 Labs) ============ -->
            <section class="section-block" id="lab-d6">
                <h3 class="section-h">H.7 Domain 6 — Monitoring, Logging &amp; Runtime Security Labs (8 labs, CKS 20%)</h3>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 6.1</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 12 min — Falco: Write Rule, Deploy, Trigger, Verify</strong><br>Write a custom Falco rule detecting <code>cat /etc/shadow</code> inside any container. Save to falco_rules.local.yaml. Validate with --dry-run. Trigger the alert. Verify it appears in /var/log/falco/alerts.log.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-yaml">- rule: Read shadow file
  desc: Detect cat /etc/shadow
  condition: spawned_process and proc.name=cat and proc.args contains /etc/shadow and container.id != host
  output: "Shadow file read! (user=%user.name container=%container.name)"
  priority: CRITICAL
  tags: [filesystem, mitre_credential_access]</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 6.2</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 8 min — Falco Exception Rule</strong><br>A monitoring agent legitimately runs <code>curl</code> every minute, triggering a Falco rule. Write an exception using append:true that excludes this specific container from the rule. Verify the exception works and other curl calls still alert.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-yaml">- rule: Launch Suspicious Network Tool in Container
  append: true
  condition: and not container.name = "monitoring-agent"</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 6.3</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 10 min — Audit Log Query: Find Suspicious Activity</strong><br>Query audit logs for: (a) all Secret reads in the last hour, (b) all failed authentication attempts, (c) any pod exec operations. Use jq. Document the queries as a runbook.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">cat /var/log/kubernetes/audit.log | jq 'select(.objectRef.resource=="secrets" and .verb=="get")'
cat /var/log/kubernetes/audit.log | jq 'select(.responseStatus.code==401)'
cat /var/log/kubernetes/audit.log | jq 'select(.objectRef.subresource=="exec")'</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 6.4</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 15 min — Incident Response Simulation</strong><br>Falco alerts: "Terminal shell in container prod/app-123". Execute the full IR playbook: (1) verify the alert, (2) contain (NetworkPolicy + cordon), (3) collect forensics (pod YAML, logs, ps, env), (4) eradicate (delete pod + SA), (5) document findings. Time: 15 minutes.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">POD=app-123; NS=prod; DIR=ir-$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M); mkdir $DIR
kubectl apply -f deny-all.yaml -n $NS  # Contain
kubectl get pod $POD -n $NS -o yaml > $DIR/pod.yaml
kubectl logs $POD -n $NS --tail=500 > $DIR/logs.txt
kubectl exec $POD -n $NS -- ps aux > $DIR/ps.txt
kubectl delete pod $POD -n $NS; kubectl delete sa app-sa -n $NS
kubectl create sa app-sa -n $NS  # Fresh SA</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 6.5</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 6 min — Falco Dry-Run Validation</strong><br>Write a Falco rule with a deliberate syntax error. Run <code>falco --dry-run</code>. Observe the error. Fix the syntax. Run --dry-run again — must pass. Restart Falco. Verify the rule is loaded: <code>falco --list | grep your-rule</code>.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">echo "bad: [syntax" >> /etc/falco/falco_rules.local.yaml
falco --dry-run  # FAILS with parser error
vi /etc/falco/falco_rules.local.yaml  # Fix syntax
falco --dry-run  # PASSES
systemctl restart falco && systemctl status falco</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 6.6</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 8 min — Trivy Operator: Deploy + Monitor</strong><br>Install Trivy Operator. Verify VulnerabilityReport CRDs are created. Check reports for a specific namespace. Identify the pod with the most CRITICAL CVEs. Recommend remediation.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-bash">kubectl apply -f ...trivy-operator.yaml
kubectl get vulnerabilityreports -A
kubectl get vulnerabilityreport -n prod -o json | jq '.items[] | {name: .metadata.labels["trivy-operator.resource.name"], critical: .report.summary.criticalCount}'</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 6.7</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 10 min — Audit Policy: Noise Reduction</strong><br>Start with an audit policy that logs everything at Metadata level. Disk fills in hours. Add rules to: (a) suppress health checks (/healthz, /readyz), (b) suppress system component reads, (c) keep Secret access at RequestResponse, (d) keep RBAC changes at RequestResponse. Verify log volume drops significantly.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-yaml">rules:
- level: None; nonResourceURLs: ["/healthz", "/readyz", "/livez"]
- level: None; users: ["system:kube-proxy", "system:apiserver"]; verbs: ["get", "list", "watch"]
- level: RequestResponse; resources: [{group: "", resources: ["secrets"]}, {group: "rbac.authorization.k8s.io", resources: ["*"]}]
- level: Metadata</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>

                <div class="exam-question-item">
                    <span class="eq-number" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#22c55e,#16a34a);">Lab 6.8</span>
                    <div class="eq-question"><strong>⏱️ 6 min — kube-bench Continuous Monitoring</strong><br>Create a CronJob that runs kube-bench weekly against all nodes. Results saved to a PVC. Configure alert if any new FAIL appears. Verify the CronJob runs successfully.</div>
                    <details><summary>Show Solution</summary><div class="eq-answer"><div class="eq-answer-label">Solution</div><pre><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: batch/v1; kind: CronJob; metadata: {name: weekly-kube-bench}
spec:
  schedule: "0 3 * * 0"
  jobTemplate:
    spec:
      template:
        spec:
          containers:
          - name: kube-bench
            image: aquasec/kube-bench:latest
            command: ["kube-bench", "run", "--targets", "master,node"]
          restartPolicy: OnFailure</code></pre></div></details>
                </div>
